(147, 29, 0, 'Instruments', '', '<p><strong>Quality, speed, and simplicity</strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>These define the core attributes of Instrumentation Laboratory products -- the most comprehensive and innovative solutions for your testing needs. Discover how our point-of-care and laboratory instruments, reagents, and data management solutions ensure quality, improve efficiency, and enhances customer care.</p>', '', 'b313d38ea8c09876915bf5d6918023b8.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 21:18:06', '2019-12-08 14:43:06', 1, '2019-12-08 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(182, 69, 0, 'Kinetic Incubating Microplate Reader ELx808IULALXH', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>1.&nbsp;Product information</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Kinetic Incubating Microplate Reader Elx808IULALXH is a multifunctional kinetic reader designed for bacterial endotoxin assay, fungi (1,3)-&szlig;-D-glucan assay and ELISA assays. The reader is a highly accurate, easy to use instrument for kinetic turbidimetric LAL assay, kinetic chromogenic LAL test&nbsp;and endpoint chromogenic LAL assay. &nbsp;Compare to kinetic incubating tube reader, the microplate reader is more efficient and is possible to be scaled up to automatic performance.</p>\r\n<p><strong>2.&nbsp;Instrumental parameters</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Wavelength range of 340-900nm, suitable for ultraviolet and visible light detection.</li>\r\n<li>6 filter wheel, standard configuration with 5 filters (340, 405, 450, 540 and 630nm).</li>\r\n<li>Temperature control range: room temperature+5â„ƒ to 50â„ƒ</li>\r\n<li>Standard curve linear correlation coefficient: |r|&ge;0.99</li>\r\n<li>Assay repeatability: CV&le;5%</li>\r\n<li>96 tests per plate</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>3. &nbsp;Application range:</strong></p>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Bacterial endotoxin (pyrogen) assay of drugs, vaccines, Water for Injection medical devices, infusion, transfusion related devices dialysate, dialysis water endotoxin testing cell suspension, cell culture media, cell culture related products recombinant protein, nucleic acid and other molecular biological products</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Endotoxin level monitoring during production: pharmaceutical raw materials, intermediate products, end product endotoxin daily monitoring.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Clinical diagnostic of sepsis and invasive fungi disease: plasma, serum, urine, cerebrospinal fluid endotoxin and (1,3)-beta-D-glucan detection.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>4.&nbsp;Ordering information</strong></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 39px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr class=\"firstRow\" style=\"height: 10px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.2459%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"139\">\r\n<p><strong>Catalog Number</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.588%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"407\">\r\n<p><strong>Description</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 29px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.2459%; height: 29px; text-align: center;\">KPR808</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 73.588%; height: 29px; text-align: justify;\">BioTek kinetic incubating microplate &nbsp; reader Elx808IULALXH for Endotoxin and &szlig;-glucan detection</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>5.&nbsp;Product qualification</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img title=\"LoA Biotek US\" src=\"/content/photo/454d33e442083bef5497bb62555d99cb.jpg\" alt=\"LoA Biotek US\" width=\"309\" height=\"424\" /></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>6. E</strong><strong>nd</strong><strong>o</strong><strong>to</strong><strong>x</strong><strong>i</strong><strong>n</strong> <strong>a</strong><strong>n</strong><strong>d </strong><strong>(</strong><strong>1,</strong><strong>3)</strong><strong>-&szlig;</strong><strong>-</strong><strong>D</strong><strong>-g</strong><strong>l</strong><strong>u</strong><strong>c</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>n</strong> <strong>as</strong><strong>s</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>y</strong> <strong>so</strong><strong>f</strong><strong>t</strong><strong>w</strong><strong>ar</strong><strong>e</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">EndoMaster<sup>TM</sup> endotoxin and &nbsp;ï¼ˆ1,3ï¼‰-&szlig;-D-glucan professional analysis software is a powerful kinetic data analysis software, which gives the user data acquisition and processing of the maximum flexibility.</p>\r\n<p>Features:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Apply to Endotoxin assay, (1,3ï¼‰-&szlig;-D-glucan assay and ELISA data analysis</li>\r\n<li>With standard version and clinical diagnostic version for the different user groups.</li>\r\n<li>Data could be output transitions and connected to the LIS system.</li>\r\n<li>Customized endotoxin test reports.</li>\r\n<li>Data analyzed by onset time, average rate, maximum rate and other methods.</li>\r\n<li>Data linear fitting or polynomial fitting.</li>\r\n<li>Real-time backup of the original data read.</li>\r\n<li>Integration of variety of kinetic microplate readers.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>7. Ordering information</strong></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.4086%; text-align: center;\"><strong>Catalog Number</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.5914%; text-align: center;\"><strong>Description</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.4086%; text-align: left;\">Gen 5</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.5914%;\">Gen5 software for BioTek ELx808IULALXH</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.4086%;\">SGen5S</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.5914%;\">Gen5 Secure software for BioTek ELx808IULALXH</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.4086%;\">EM01</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 72.5914%;\">Endotoxin and (1,3)-&szlig;-D-glucan assay software EndoMaster</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>', '', '9510c9297643f790532d2486d424b48e.jpg', '', '2019-10-20 17:47:31', '2020-02-03 18:09:19', 1, '2020-02-03 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(131, 52, 0, 'Dip Slide', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A&nbsp;<strong>dip slide</strong>&nbsp;(or&nbsp;<strong>dipslide</strong>) is a test for the presence of&nbsp;microorganisms<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">&nbsp;</span>in&nbsp;liquids. The use of dip slides is the method most frequently used to measure and observe microbial activity in liquid-based systems. It is often used in testing cooling systems. Dip slides are often used to determine the presence of slime forming bacteria in cooling &amp; industrial water systems.&nbsp;The Health and Safety Executive\'s&nbsp;(HSE) recommends the use of dipslides to monitor the general activity of aerobic bacteria.&nbsp;The dip slide test consists of a sterile&nbsp;culture medium,&nbsp;on a plastic carrier that is dipped into the liquid to be sampled.&nbsp;The culture is then incubated, allowing for microbial growth.&nbsp;Most Dip slides consist of 1 - 2 agars attached to a flexible plastic paddle, this allows full contact of the agar onto the desired area for testing.&nbsp;Most Dipslides come in a circular clear shatterproof tube that can be inserted into a dip-slide incubator.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Most Dip slides are&nbsp;incubated&nbsp;at 30<sup>o</sup>C for 48 hours after being dipped into the sample to ensure that the results are accurate. Some dipslides require different temperatures and incubation times depending on the type of agar used, and which organism is being tested for. After being dipped into the sample the dip slide is returned and secured in its original container for the incubation process. Multiple tests at varying periods are recommended to increase accuracy. It is important that&nbsp;biocides&nbsp;are not applied to the water prior to testing as this would significantly alter the results.&nbsp;The&nbsp;clarity&nbsp;of the sample is not necessarily reflective of the presence of&nbsp;bacteria&nbsp;as seemingly clear water may still have bacteria present. For some water systems a weekly dip slide test is recommended. For multiple tests the&nbsp;incubation period&nbsp;and&nbsp;temperature&nbsp;should be the same each time a new sample is assessed. Bacteria present in the sample liquid will grow and form colonies. A bacterial reference chart is used to determine the number of bacteria in the sample. Appropriate treatment is applied to the water source once abnormal levels of bacterial activity are noticed. Once water treatment is effective the bacterial count produced by the dip slide test should be low, approximately &lt;10<sup>4</sup>.&nbsp;Dip slides are normally used when microbiological activity is relatively high (1,000 - 100,000&nbsp;CFU&nbsp;per milliliter of water).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The dip slide results should be used only as a guide as the accuracy of the dip slide is limited as a result of the small sample size that is analyzed and the method used to obtain results. Nevertheless, dip slides may be very useful as they are very convenient, simple to use and cost effective.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>For inquiry please kindly email to : lisa@prolabios.com</strong></p>', '', 'd2bbed3955aedc94bd61d2e1c45c5d89.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 17:33:32', '2020-03-08 20:23:52', 1, '2020-03-08 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(134, 54, 0, 'Biological Indicators', '', '<p>A Biological Indicator (BI) is a well-characterized preparation of a specific microorganism with known resistance to aspesific sterilization process (USP Biological Indicators - Resistance Performance Tests).</p>\r\n<p>BIs are regulated by:&nbsp;<strong>ISO 111-1:2017</strong> Sterilization of health care product -- Biological Indicators -- Part 1: <strong>General requirements. USP pharmacopeia &nbsp;</strong>Biological Indicator for sterilization.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>A BI is ready for use microbiological test system, consisting of spores that are added to a carrier (suspension, paper strip, glass, plastic or other) packed to&nbsp;maintain the integrity and the viability of inoculated carrier.</p>\r\n<p>Microorganisms widely recognized as suitable for biological indicator are spore-forming bactreia, more resistant than microflora:</p>\r\n<p>- <em>Geobacillus stearothermophillus</em> (steam, hydrogen peroxide sterilization)</p>\r\n<p>- <em>Bacillus athropeus</em> (dry heat, ethylene oxide sterilization)</p>\r\n<p>- <em>Bacillus pumilus</em> (gamma irradiation sterilization).</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;<img src=\"/content/photo/c7ef1660ebd469d6e2ca867cecde7a40_thm.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></p>\r\n<p>If the spores grow after a sterilization cycle the process is considered to have failed. On the contrary the sterilization process turns out to be successful if spores are completely killed after the sterilization cycle.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>For inquiry please kindly email to : lisa@prolabios.com</strong></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '', 'eeae2c4a957d3d07049ec07e9e028fc5.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 17:52:02', '2020-03-08 20:23:41', 1, '2020-03-08 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(125, 63, 0, 'Liquid Handling', '', '<p>The specialists&rsquo; choice for contamination free Media dispensing. Peristaltic pumps dedicated for sterile microbiological and cell culture Media filling. Full metal body, no rims no gaps &ndash; Ideal for food and pharmaceutical Labs. User friendly command spread sheet makes it easy for everybody to program the pump upon his needs</p>', '', '7903fab0fbc13b121dfa487a09a017df.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 15:49:46', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 1, '2019-08-25 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(38, 4, 2, 'Visit Our Booth at R01 at LabIndonesia 22-24 April 2020', 'PJT 2 Ensure Water Supply Baku to Jakarta, please.', '<div class=\"\"><strong>22-24 April 2020</strong> <strong>PT. Prolabios Mitra Analitika</strong><span class=\"\"><strong> will exhibit at LabIndonesia 2020</strong> at Jakarta Convention Center, Jakarta. <strong>PT. Prolabios Mitra Analitika\'s booth no. R01 Hall B.</strong></span></div>\r\n<p>LabIndonesia is Indonesia&rsquo;s only trade show dedicated to laboratory equipment and services, connecting lab operators, decision makers, and suppliers from around the world in one comprehensive event. Since the first edition in 2010, LabIndonesia has grown significantly, with a significant 29% growth in visitor attendance in the most recent edition. Apart from the exhibition segment, LabIndonesia is also co-located with the conferences &amp; workshops which is organized by associations &amp; government bodies, as well as over hundreds of technical seminars, workshops, and product demonstrations conducted by subject matter experts from around the world.</p>\r\n<p><img title=\"LabIndonesia 2020\" src=\"/content/photo/c4cdd0da37725664a9c3870c71180400.jpg\" alt=\"LabIndonesia 2020\" width=\"650\" height=\"325\" /></p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Public Company Jasa Tirta 2 (PJT-2) said that the reliability of the Jatiluhur reservoir to supply water to Jakarta is still relatively safe. supply water diverted to Jakarta monitored every day, and on the conditions accepted by August 29, 2016 in Jakarta 16.67 cubic meters per second (M3 / sec), consisting of catch (intake) potty 6.04 m3 / s, Pulogadung Buaran 4.25 and 6.38. This came during a meeting of visits BRPAM work to PJT-2, on Monday (8/30/2016) ago. At the meeting was informed that PJT-2 is capable of supplying water to the raw water Jakarta when development occurs Water Treatment Plant (IPA) in Buaran (ie Buaran 3).<br />&nbsp;<br />BRPAM Working Visit to PJT-2, intended to determine the condition of PJT-2 in the supply of raw water to taps in Jakart and strategy planning come. The visit was led by Donna Ria BRPAM Silaen, Chairman, Members disampingi by BRPAM, Ferdy B. Madian and Dormaringan Saragih, accompanied by Specialist Engineering BRPAM, Tatit Palgunadi and Camelia Murniwati. Tim BRPAM accepted by the Director of PJT-2, Djoko Saputro, disampingi by Harry M. Indeed Operations Director and the General Manager and other staff. The meeting was conducted at the Central Office PJT-2, which is located in Jatiluhur, Purwakarta.<br />&nbsp;<br />In his introduction, the Chairman expressed his gratitude for BRPAM for the welcome PJT-2 and explain the condition of the water supply in Jakarta as well as some issues that need to be addressed now and in the future.<br />&nbsp; <br />Exposure to water reliability condition to Jakarta from PJT-2 delivered by Reni, Division of Water Resources and Electricity, stated that for the needs Jakarta water is channeled through the West Tarum Canal (STB) is the division of Dam Juanda do in Curug area. Capacity per 08.29.2016 capable STB holds 48.67 m3 / sec, which is allocated for the irrigation needs of agriculture, industry and raw water for drinking water. \"Until now, the water supply to Jakarta from the WTC still relatively safe \"said Reni. In the discussion session discussed some things about strategies and plans PJT-2 forward. SPAM plan Jatiluhur and plans PJT II in supplying the bulk water. PJT II deliver additional supply of raw water channeled through STB to Jakarta for 5 m3 / second for 3 Buaran IPA plan may still be made. This is reinforced by the presence of Syphon Bekasi, normalization program WTC and development plans Syphon Cikarang. That the reservoir has entered into Presidential Decree No. 3 of 2016 on Accelerating the Implementation of Strategic Projects National. In the future policy strategy, PJT II will supply bulk water to Jakarta. The bulk water supply is expected to help Jakarta increase the coverage pelayanannya.Saat provide insight into the drinking water service in Jakarta, PJT II hope NRW (Non Revenue Water) drinking water services Jakarta could diturunkansehingga raw water supplied can be more widely used by customers in the form of clean water.<br /><br />After discussion, the Day of the same, BRPAM accompanied by the Manager and technical team PJT II also conducted field visits to Ir. H. Juanda, Curug weir and Syphon Cibeet. Ir. H. Juanda is a series of terraced pengliaran (cascade) along with Saguling and Reservoir Cirata. The water in the three reservoirs will come from the Citarum River. Juanda reservoir volume of water applied to the raw water requirement of Jakarta is 6% of the entire water from the Citarum River is controlled by PJT II. In the dividends Curug weir flow of water that is to SaluranTarum West, North SaluranTarum, and SaluranTarumTimur. At Curug weir, the water in the pump using a hydraulic pump to the WTC. on location Syphon visit Cibeet, obtained information that Syphon Cibeet built to avoid the mixing of water from the river to the water channel Cibeet Tarum Barat, so the quality, quantity and continuity of raw water is maintained. Currently Syphon Cibeet been equipped with bangunanTrash Rake function to filter and lift garbage darialiransungai. Trash Rake is still in the testing phase and has not been handed over to PJT-2.<br /><br />During the field visit, BRPAM also provide some input to be considered in monitoring water quality, among other things the need for monitoring industrial waste, domestic effluent and dissemination of awareness to the community to keep the drains. (# CIM / dhs)</p>', '641d871229b477d50bf2a244d4e5bdf9.jpg', '', '2016-09-05 02:33:48', '2020-02-03 23:57:31', 3, '2020-02-03 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(189, 74, 0, 'bioall - Bio Safety Cabinet (BSC) and Laminar Flow Cabinet (LFC)', '', '<h4 class=\"h2_tit\"><strong>CHC LAB - South Korea, bioall : Bio Safety Cabinet (BSC) and Laminar Flow Cabinet (LFC)</strong></h4>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Full line up</strong> : Configure product full line up required for biotechnology</p>\r\n<p><strong>The safety of researchers comes first</strong>: Biometric Safety Workstation puts priority on protecting researchers and environmental safety and samples from biological high-risk groups.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Delivering the Best Service</strong>: With 100% bioall technology, the company obtained overseas certification for the first time in Korea and solved unnecessary price bubbles by manufacturing in Korea. We train NSF Certifier of national oil to quickly and accurately deliver the best service to the installation and verification operation of equipment.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"/content/photo/34aad7849477969e7fab2c9cf03f23e0.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"545\" height=\"216\" /><img src=\"/content/photo/a3044d6fb41ff4ef5faeea78b512646e.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"581\" height=\"260\" /></p>', '', '297e80914d279ccfea64d5e6118b066b.jpg', '', '2020-02-04 00:52:36', '2020-02-04 01:35:28', 1, '2020-02-04 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `web_content` (`content_id`, `channel_id`, `content_cat_id`, `title`, `title_eng`, `description`, `description_eng`, `file`, `file_eng`, `posted`, `updated`, `status`, `published`, `type`, `param1`, `param2`, `param3`, `ispromo`) VALUES
(32, 4, 5, 'ISO 11133:2014 Preparation, Production, Storage and Performance Testing of Culture Media', 'PAM JAYA AND OPERATORS PARTNERS  COMMITMENTS TO KEEP WATER OF JAKARTA', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">ISO 11133:2014 Microbiology of food, animal feed and water &mdash; Preparation, production, storage and performance testing of culture media</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ISO 11133:2014 standard &ldquo;Microbiology of food, animal feed and water &minus; Preparation, production, storage and performance testing of culture media&rdquo;, replaces previous standards and aims at enhancing the reliability of microbiological analyses by standardizing the quality and performance testing of culture media dedicated to microbiological analyses of food and water.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These requirements are applicable to all categories of culture media prepared for use in laboratories performing microbiological analyses.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This International Standard also sets criteria and describes methods for the performance testing of culture media. This International Standard applies to producers such as:<br />- commercial bodies producing and/or distributing ready-to-use or semi-finished reconstituted or dehydrated media;<br />- non-commercial bodies supplying media to third parties;<br />- microbiological laboratories preparing culture media for their own use.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In May 2014, the International Organization for Standardization (ISO) published the revised EN ISO 11133, which is now a full standard and as such mandatory for all accredited laboratories that perform microbiological testing of food, animal feed or water using culture media. It has been completely restructured, clarifying procedures and drawing a clear line between the responsibilities of the laboratories and the manufacturers/suppliers of culture media. The ultimate aim of the new standard is to further improve the safety of the food and beverage products we consume.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>1. What is the new standard?</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The new EN ISO 11133:2014 Quality-assured culture media for food and water testing to enhance consumer safety The one-part EN ISO 11133:2014, titled &ldquo;Microbiology of food, animal feed and water &ndash; preparation, production, storage and performance testing of culture media&rdquo;, was compiled by a joint ISO working group from food and water standardization. It applies to culture media intended for the microbiological analysis of food for human consumption, animal feed and samples from the manufacturing environment of such products, as well as of all kinds of water for consumption or use in food production. It covers all culture media formats, ranging from dehydrated and ready-to-use media for classical microbiological methods to media for alternative testing techniques.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>2. What are the objectives of the standard?</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">There are two guiding principles in this regulation: Media preparation and performance testing. For example, very practical guidance is provided for the testing of water quality for media preparation, pH adjustments, storage of prepared plates, tubes and bottles.<br /><br />The second guiding principle is that performance testing conditions should resemble the intended sample testing conditions as closely as possible, leading to more accurate and meaningful results. As a consequence, culture media for quantitative testing must now be tested quantitatively, and those used in conjunction with membrane filters must be tested in combination with these filters. Another objective is to specify the requirements in more detail and describe the practical aspects. Step-by-step instructions, complemented by flow charts, are provided for performing and evaluating performance tests. The standard contains comprehensive tables for the specifications for most culture media, not only for food but now for water microbiology as well.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>3. What has been included in the new standard?</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In addition to the medium&rsquo;s target microorganism and the relevant ISO standard, these tables show each medium&rsquo;s functions to be tested (productivity, selectivity, specificity), the appropriate control strains for these functions, including their World Data Centre for Microorganisms (WDCM) numbers, as well as the test criteria and/or characteristic reactions and other practical information. EN ISO 11133 now also contains hands-on, detailed instructions for the maintenance of microbial strains as well as the preparation and standardization of working cultures and inoculation suspensions. The standard specifies the optimal number of colony forming units (cfu) per plate or membrane filter and describes how productivity ratios and limits are determined.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>4. What does this change mean for labs?</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">An ever-increasing number of laboratories source their culture media from suppliers to simplify their workflows and ensure high quality and batch-to-batch consistency of the media they use. EN ISO 11133:2014 takes account of this development by stipulating requirements not only for laboratories that prepare their media in-house but also for manufacturers. With a clear line drawn between the quality assurance responsibilities of users and suppliers, lab managers can now reliably assess which duties and responsibilities no longer apply when they decide to procure culture media. For labs that produce their own culture media, it is usually sufficient to test each batch with a single test strain named in the standard, whereas manufacturers are expected to perform tests using several microorganisms. However, both labs must meet the specified productivity and selectivity to a level as described for each test organism.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>5. Are extensive tests required by all labs?</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">For all ISO 11133:2014 compliant culture media they provide, suppliers need to conduct rigorous qualitative and/or quantitative testing. However, ready-to-use media allow laboratories to rely on the performance tests that the manufacturer conducts as long as the transport conditions are observed and the manufacturer&rsquo;s QC test is performed according to the requirements of EN ISO 11133. The end user needs to make sure that testing was performed according to the requirements of the standard. A supporting document that the manufacturer provides to the end user is the quality control certificate. It discloses the test organisms used, the inoculation levels, the acceptance criteria of the performance tests and the test results.<br /><br /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Each production lot of Liofilchem media is accurately tested for growth promotion, sterility and reproducibility with a schedule that includes the microbial strains indicated in the standard, therefore simplifying the amount of validation customers have to do in their own laboratories on each lot of ready-to-use media.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The QC certificates have been progressively updated and contain the statement &ldquo;Tested according to EN ISO 11133&rdquo;, to show and guarantee reliable results and batch-to-batch media consistency.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As Liofilchem manufactures ready-to-use culture media using its own dehydrated culture media, its stringent system of procedures for conformity to the technical specifications and control testing can be followed through the entire production process making full traceability easier.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The full compliance of Liofilchem to ISO 11133:2014 standard, in addition to the ISO 9001 and ISO 13485 certifications, reinforces its position as one of the world class leading manufacturers of diagnostics for microbiology.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Took place in Penang Bistro Restaurant, Kebon Sirih Jakata, PDAM Jaya and Operator Partners (PALYJA and AETRA) held Halal bi halal with people from media agency. Thursday (7/21/2016) ago. Halal bi halal, which is packaged in a relaxed dialogue event, on the theme Keeping Air Jakarta, filled with discussions related&nbsp;the water supply in Jakarta. Speakers discussion is Erlan Hidayat, PAM Jaya president director; Mohammad Selim, President Aetra; Budi Susilo, Director&nbsp;CS Palyja; and Agus Pambudio, observers of public services as a moderator. In such event, PAM Jaya and invites various agencies Partners&nbsp;Related to expand the partnership to improve services and access to clean water for all citizens of Jakarta. It was explained that the development progress Jakata&nbsp;followed by population growth, resulting in ever-increasing need for clean water, but otherwise the raw water supply is not met. \"Demandclean water in Jakarta reached 26,100 liters per second, while the supply is only up to 15,000 liters per second, so there is 9,100 liters per defisi tsebesar&nbsp;second, \"said Erlan Hidayat. It added that 96% of raw water to meet the needs of the city of Jakarta (81% comes from Jatiluhur through open channels River&nbsp;Tarum Barat and another 15% comes from Air Munitions Prepared purchased from PDAM Tangerang District). The remaining 4% additional raw water from rivers in Jakarta.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">PAM JAYA together PALYJA and AETRA continuously make efforts in order to fulfill the needs of drinking water for residents of Jakarta. PALYJA as&nbsp;one of the Drinking Water Operator Partners did make every effort and resources in fulfilling the needs of drinking water to prove his commitment to&nbsp;Low-Income Communities (MBR) to provide 245 public hydrants to serve 73,500 residents plus 58 Kiosks Water and Master Meter to&nbsp;serves 70,000 residents in various areas in the western part of Jakarta. \"In a period of 17 years (1998-2015), has served 404 769 PALYJA customer connections,&nbsp;with 160.3juta m3 volume sold, up 73.15% of the population access and reach 39.3% Non Revenue Water (NRW) said Budi Susilo, from PALYJA. Budi added,&nbsp;PALYJA investment amount from the year 1998 - 2015 to reach Rp. 2,089 trillion by targeting services, clean water sales and technology transfer.Such investments could increase access for the poor community. \"Based on data from customer growth PALYJA of the year 1998-2015, income people&nbsp;Low served rose to 571% \", added Budi.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Likewise also the AETRA, as one of the Partners has been adding clean water coverage in the eastern part of Jakarta, especially in hard water areas. \"AETRA add more than 120 new connections in areas cut off in the village Rorotan RW 08 and 09 as a result of the work&nbsp;East Flood Canal \"said Selim, President Director of PT. Aetra Air Jakarta (AETRA) .AETRA will provide access to clean water in Rusunawa Rawa Bebek, Semper Timur, JakartaEast, by optimizing the fulfillment of the supply for the occupants Rusunawa of 32.400 m3 / month or 12.50 liters per second .In the first half of 2016, AETRA increasing the number of customers experiencing more than 7,000 customers .. \"AETRA also adding New Connection Program with the implementation of the Program BACAN is an abbreviation of Pay Air Price Beautiful and Installment Program to Ease new connections \", said Selim.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a moment of intimacy atmosphere Halal PAM Jaya and Partners, PAM JAYA Jakarta urged citizens to be able to contribute to maintain the availability of water to keep&nbsp;cleanliness of rivers in Jakarta as a potential source of raw water and use water sparingly and wisely. Expected partnership that exists for&nbsp;between the government and the private sector can be a solution for the problem of clean water in Jakarta. In a question and answer session, media players dig deeper into Jakarta plans for fulfillment of raw water, the continuation of PAM Jaya and carrier partners, and the incorporation of PAM Jaya - PDPAL. Reporters also undergo an interview with the&nbsp; various resource persons who attended the Halal Bi halal. Donna Silaen, Chairman of BRPAM, appreciate the media meeting. Also present at this event, the ranks PAM JAYA Directors, Board of Directors PALYJA, Directors and Senior Manager AETRA, Director of PD. PAL, Chairman and Members of the Regulatory Board and the Board members<br />Supervisors. (# KMS / dhs)</p>', 'c9adcf113311aa6d971e9cdfef63a8bb.jpg', '', '2016-08-04 05:18:50', '2020-06-16 18:53:17', 3, '2016-07-27 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(33, 4, 0, 'Technical Training About Endotoxin Detection at Bioendo', 'Safari Ramadhan 2016 PALYJA with Committee of Drinking Water Customers', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">To assist our foreign agents to offer more professional technical support for final users, We, Bioendo, manufacturer of amebocyte lysate and endotoxin assay kit, has held technical training on endotoxin detection for foreign agents. The training provided opportunities for our agents to learn knowledge of lyophilized amebocyte lysate and BET operation. We will continue to provide technical service and training for our agents in future.</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the moment of the month of fasting, a month full of grace, together PALYJA PAM Jaya, BRPAM establish a relationship with your customersï¿½ drinking water, in the activities of Safari Ramadan 2016. Ramadan Safari do PALYJA in meeting customers\' drinking water in this case represented by the Committee on Drinking Water Customers (KPAM) Palyja service area, located in the area Bendungan Hilir, Jakarta, on Thursday (23.06.16). Meyritha Maryanie, CSSR and Corporate Communication Palyja in the opening said that the relationship with the customer Palyja, as operator of drinking water, intended to build partnerships and relationships better in the drinking water service, hoping that KPAM, as customers increasingly active representatives in the activities of customers, both in terms of monitoring customer complaints, socialization, communication and coordination.<br /><br />Dormaringan H. Saragih, BRPAM Members, who attended the Safari Ramadhan, KPAM convey important role in building water service performance drink a positive and better in Jakarta. Confirmed by Dorman, nicknames Dormaringan, order in planning and pelaksanana KPAM activities remain pay attention to aspects of the process, substance, reports and strategic role. Explained, the question is that KPAM running the appropriate process agreed by KPAM, PALYJA and BRPAM; the substance is so KPAM set charge information and material submitted by the operator (in this case PALYJA) context and situation of local communities in the region KPAM. \"For example in the North is the issue of handling the illegal connection, in the South of the user ground water, and so on at the Centre. Fathers are of KPAM better understand the information needs what is required by the customer \"Dorman explained.In terms of the report, Dorman also requested that KPAM orderly in reporting and customer participation in any socialization. Associated with strategic role,Dorman asserted the existence KPAM should become the frontline for BRPAM to menginverisasi, identification and communication services in the customer\'s drinking water.\"When the service was less than satisfactory, KPAM was the first should know, and vice versa if the service is satisfactory, KPAM who expressed his appreciation. so that existence amid customer feels \"Dorman explained.<br /><br />In line with Dorman, Budi Susilo, Director of Customer Service and Commercial Palyja, said that KPAM is an important instrument for service water in Jakarta. Added by Budi, that is currently being invested PALYJA and construction of water supply infrastructure in order to improve Jakarta water services.<br />ï¿½<br />In that event, H.Nur, KPAM Central Jakarta to appreciate the initiative PALYJA to keep KPAM and establish a relationship with the customer, while hoping that the board KPAM remain faithful in service and improve its performance. The same is conveyed by the representative of North Jakarta KPAM explain things that have been done menjembati KPAM for the benefit of customers and operators. Various input and views of the audience into information it is important to enhance the role and function of KPAM.<br /><br />The event, which lasted until the evening was joyful along with door prize comes also with singing and music. (#DHS).</p>', 'dc384067a664aebec6fac21c1c66689b.jpg', '', '2016-08-04 17:28:32', '2019-10-18 16:00:47', 3, '2016-06-30 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 1),
(128, 53, 0, 'Food Safety', '', '<p>Rapid tests for the detection of a range of bacteria from work surfaces, the processing environment and finished product.</p>\r\n<p>All three systems utilise an identical test principle. Bacteria are recovered from the surface of food manufacturing or processing equipment using a pre-moistened swab, which is capable of neutralising commonly employed detergents and sanitisers. The sample swab is then transferred into an organism specific media (swabs have a conveniently located break point so that they can easily be broken off into the growth media). Following incubation, if the specific target bacteria are present on the sample swabs, bacterial growth will cause the colour of the media to change.</p>\r\n<p>Range products for Food Safety:</p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 659px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 29px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 29px;\"><strong>Catalogue</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; text-align: center; height: 29px;\"><strong>Product</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: center; height: 29px;\"><strong>Application</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">71680</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">FOOD SYSTEM</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px;\">Direct Identification of the main pathogenic microorganisms from Foodstuffs. Validated to ISO 16140: Microbiology of food and animal feeding stuffs: protocol for the validation of alternative methods (<em>Listeria spp.</em> &amp; <em>Salmonella spp.</em>)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">71655</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">HACCP SYSTEM Plus</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px;\">Total bacterial count and direct Identification of the main pathogenic microorganisms from Surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">79700</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">MAIA Pesticide MultiTest</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px;\">Colorimetric system for the detection of organophosphate, organochloride and carbamate pesticide residues in water, food and drink.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">80356</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">MeRA Test</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Microbiological test with spores of <em>Geobacillus stearothermophilus</em> for the detection of antimicrobial agent residues in meat.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">80355</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">MiRA Test</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Microbiological test with spores of <em>Geobacillus stearothermophilus</em> for the detection of antimicrobial agent residues in milk.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">86001</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">CLEAN TEST</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">CLEAN TEST is a swab for the detection of protein, fat and sugar residues suitable for the check of work surfaces cleaning level.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">86102</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Contam Swab Listeria</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px;\">CONTAM SWAB - LISTERIA is a swab containing a culture medium used for the detection of Listeria spp. directly<br />from surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">86101</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Contam Swab <em>E. coli</em>-coliforms</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px;\">CONTAM SWAB - <em>E.coli</em>/coliform is a microbiological test with chromogenic culture medium for the detection of <em>Escherichia</em><br /><em>coli</em> and other coliform directly from surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">86103</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 54px; text-align: left;\">Contam Swab <em>Salmonella</em></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 54px; text-align: justify;\">CONTAM SWAB - <em>SALMONELLA</em> is a microbiological test with a selective and differential medium for the detection of <em>Salmonella spp.</em> directly from surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\">86100</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 54px;\">Contam Swab Contamination</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: justify; height: 54px;\">CONTAM SWAB - CONTAMINATION is a microbiological test with culture medium and growth indicator (TTC) for the microbial load assay directly from surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\">86105</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 54px;\">Contam Swab Yeasts &amp; Moulds</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 54px;\">CONTAM SWAB - Yeasts/Moulds is a swab containing a culture medium used for the detection of yeasts and moulds directly<br />from surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">85601</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">ESC Swab Neutralizing Rinse Solution 10 mL</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">ESC (Easy Surface Checking) swab - Neutralizing Rinse Solution is a device used for the microbiological monitoring of<br />surfaces by swab sampling method. Neutralizing agents included in the medium allow to assess the effectiveness of sanitization procedures in areas where residual disinfectants are presumably present.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">85603</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">ESC Swab Buffered Peptone Water 10 mL</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">ESC (Easy Surface Checking) swab - Buffered Peptone Water is a device used for the microbiological monitoring of surfaces<br />by swab sampling method. The medium is recommended for the detection and enumeration of <em>Salmonella spp</em>, Enterobacteriaceae and <em>Listeria spp</em> within foodstuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">85605</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">ESC Swab D/E Neutralizing Broth 10 mL</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">ESC (Easy Surface Checking) swab - D/E Neutralizing Broth is a device used for the microbiological monitoring of surfaces by swab sampling method. Neutralizing agents included in the medium allow to assess the effectiveness of sanitization procedures in areas where residual disinfectants are presumably present. D/E Neutralizing Broth inactivates higher<br />concentrations of residual antimicrobials when compared with other standard neutralizing formulations.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">85607</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">ESC Swab Letheen Broth 10 mL</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">ESC (Easy Surface Checking) swab - Letheen Broth is a device used for the microbiological monitoring of surfaces by swab sampling method. Neutralizing agents included in the medium allow to assess the effectiveness of sanitization procedures in areas where residual disinfectants are presumably present. Letheen Broth is recommended by the AOAC for determining the phenol coefficient of cationic surfactants.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">85609</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">ESC Swab Maximum Recovery Diluent 10 mL</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">ESC (Easy Surface Checking) swab - Maximum Recovery Diluent is a device used for the microbiological monitoring of surfaces by swab sampling method. The medium, also referred to as Peptone Salt Solution, is a protective and isotonic diluent for maximum recovery of organisms from various sources. Its formula complies with ISO 6887 for the microbiological examination of food and animal feeding stuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">96762</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Sampling Template 10x10 Sterile</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px;\">Sampling Template 10x10 is a sterile plastic device used to delimit an area of 100 cm2.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">85270</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Sterile Swab in Envelope</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">STERILE SWABS WITH ENVELOPE are constituted by sterile dry swabs inserted in a tube and endowed with a cap which hermetically closes the neck of the tube, so avoiding contamination of the tube and protecting user&rsquo;s hands. Sterilization is assured by irradiation at 2.5 Mrad rays. Each tube containing a swab is inserted into a thermically soldered bag.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">85275</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Sterile Swab without envelope</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">STERILE SWABS WITHOUT ENVELOPE are constituted by sterile dry swabs inserted in a tube and endowed with a cap which hermetically closes the neck of the tube, so avoiding contamination of the tube and protecting user&rsquo;s hands. Sterilization is assured by irradiation at 2.5 Mrad rays.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">499010</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Listeria U.V.M. Broth Bag</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">LISTERIA UVM MOD BROTH &ndash; BAG is a ready to use liquid medium in bag for the selective enrichment of <em>Listeria monocytogenes</em> according to the International Dairy Federation (IDF). The bags can be placed on special supports, connected to sterile tubes with the aid of specific joints and used with diluters, peristaltic pumps o, simply, you can bring the liquid to fall.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">499020</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Listeria Demi Fraser Broth Bag</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">LISTERIA DEMI FRASER BROTH &ndash; BAG is a ready to use liquid medium in bag for enrichment of <em>Listeria monocytogenes</em> in foods according to ISO 11290. The bags can be placed on special supports, connected to sterile tubes with the aid of specific joints and used with diluters, peristaltic pumps o, simply, you can bring the liquid to fall.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">499030</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Buffered Peptone Water Bag</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">BUFFERED PEPTONE WATER &ndash; BAG is a ready to uese liquid medium in bag for the pre-enrichment of <em>Salmonella spp</em>. in food according to ISO 6579. The bags can be placed on special supports, connected to sterile tubes with the aid of specific joints and used with diluters, peristaltic pumps o, simply, you can bring the liquid to fall.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">499040</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Maximum Recovery Diluent Bag</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Maximum Recovery Diluent (Peptone Salt Solution) is a protective and isotonic diluent used to maximize the recovery of microorganisms in the preparation of the initial suspension and decimal dilutions of test samples. This solution complies with the recommendations of ISO 6887 for the microbiological examination of food.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">499060</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Tryptic Soy Broth Bag</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Ready to use liquid medium in PVC bag of 3 liters for microbial growth.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">PC010</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">PATH-CHEK Coliform Detection Broth (3 ml)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">A range of swabs for the detection of coliforms from environmental surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">PC080</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">PATH-CHEK Listeria Detection Broth (3 ml)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">A range of swabs for the detection of <em>Listeria</em> from environmental surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">PC020</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">PATH-CHEK Salmonella Detection Broth (3 ml)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">A range of swabs for the detection of <em>Salmonella</em> from environmental surfaces.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">PCS100</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">PATH-CHEK Pre-moistened Swabs</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Pre-moistened swabs increase recovery from wet and dry surfaces. Also neutralises residual detergents and sanitising agents, preserving target microorganisms</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.2096%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">PC006-100</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 31.7764%; height: 18px;\">Path- Chek Hygiene Protein</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 53.0938%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">A rapid test for the detection of food residues from environmental surfaces or processing equipment.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>For inquiry please kindly email to : lisa@prolabios.com</strong></p>', '', 'c3c6473547a5e8ce588b848ce35b96e1.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 17:12:01', '2020-03-08 20:24:20', 1, '2020-03-08 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(124, 55, 0, 'Ready To Use Cultured Media', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Since 1983 Liofilchem&reg; has committed its own Research &amp; Development department in the production of high quality and reliable microbiology products. Our dedication to Customer satisfaction and exceptional manufacturing versatility have granted Liofilchem continuous growth, as a result of the increasing quality of our products and the worldwide distribution of the Liofilchem &reg; brand name. Liofilchem&reg; currently has over 100 employees, including direct scientific and commercial representatives. The complete manufacturing processes and quality control are carried out in house by our staff at our two facilities in Roseto degli Abruzzi of total over 7000 m<sup>2</sup> area. The newest of them was opened in August 2010 and represents the state-of-the-art for the diagnostic manufacturing.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Liofilchem&reg; produces a variety of chromogenic media of its own formulation, called Chromatic&trade;, in continuous expansion. Available as both dehydrated format and ready to use in petri dish or bottle.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Contact plates 55 mm</strong><br />Available in double or triple envelop, gamma or beta irradiated, packed either singularly intransparent peelable blister or in pile. Manufactured under the maximum hygiene control: A grade Clean Room.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; padding-left: 160px;\"><img src=\"/content/photo/181d65d2b797898a5f3af76e6177d9e8.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"162\" height=\"121\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>For inquiry please kindly email to : lisa@prolabios.com</strong></p>', '', '970653107b9571008225cf46338cc564.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 15:17:38', '2020-03-08 20:25:33', 1, '2020-03-08 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(135, 27, 0, 'Microbiology', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Microbiology</strong>Â (from GreekÂ <span lang=\"grc\" title=\"Ancient Greek language text\">Î¼á¿‘ÎºÏÎ¿Ï‚</span>,Â <em>mÄ«kros</em>, \"small\";Â <span lang=\"grc\" title=\"Ancient Greek language text\">Î²Î¯Î¿Ï‚</span>,Â <em>bios</em>, \"life\"; andÂ <span lang=\"grc\" title=\"Ancient Greek language text\">-Î»Î¿Î³Î¯Î±</span>,Â <em>-logia</em>) is the study of microorganisms, those beingÂ unicellularÂ (single cell),Â multicellularÂ (cell colony), orÂ acellularÂ (lacking cells).<sup id=\"cite_ref-Brock_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microbiology#cite_note-Brock-1\">]</a></sup>Â Microbiology encompasses numerous sub-disciplines includingÂ virology,Â parasitology,Â micologyÂ andÂ bacteriology.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">EukaryoticÂ microorganisms possess membrane-bound cellÂ organellesÂ and includeÂ fungiÂ andÂ protists, whereasÂ prokaryoticÂ organismsâ€”all of which are microorganismsâ€”are conventionally classified as lacking membrane-bound organelles and includeÂ BacteriaÂ andÂ Arachea. Microbiologists traditionally relied on culture, staining, and microscopy. However, less than 1% of the microorganisms present in common environments can be cultured in isolation using current means.Â Microbiologists often rely on molecular biology tools such as DNA sequence based identification, for example 16s rRNA gene sequence used for bacteria identification.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">VirusesÂ have been variably classified as organisms, as they have been considered either as very simple microorganisms or very complex molecules.Â Prions, never considered as microorganisms, have been investigated by virologists, however, as the clinical effects traced to them were originally presumed due to chronic viral infections, and virologists took searchâ€”discovering \"infectious proteins\".</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The existence of microorganisms was predicted many centuries before they were first observed, for example by the Jains in India and byÂ Marcus Terentius Varro in ancient Rome. The first recorded microscope observation was of the fruiting bodies of moulds, byÂ Robert HookeÂ in 1666, but the Jesuit priest Athanasius KircherÂ was likely the first to see microbes, which he mentioned observing in milk and putrid material in 1658. Antonie van LeeuwenhoekÂ is considered a father of microbiologyÂ as he observed and experimented with microscopic organismsÂ in 1676, using simple microscopesÂ of his own design. Scientific microbiology developed in the 19th century through the work of Louis PasteurÂ and in medical microbiology Robert Koch.</p>', '', '79054cf366d982e6090dd4229f187aa0.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 19:01:48', '2019-08-25 19:03:04', 1, '2019-08-25 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(136, 57, 0, 'Immunology', '', '<p style=\"background: white; margin: 6pt 0cm; text-align: justify;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">Immunology</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">Â is a branch ofÂ <a title=\"Biology\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biology\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">biology</span></a>Â that covers the study ofÂ <a title=\"Immune system\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immune_system\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">immune systems</span></a>Â in allÂ <a title=\"Organism\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organism\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">organisms</span></a>.</span><sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" style=\"unicode-bidi: isolate;\"></sup><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">Â Immunology charts, measures, and contextualizes theÂ <a title=\"Physiology\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physiology\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">physiological</span></a>Â functioning of the immune system in states of both health and diseases; malfunctions of the immune system in immunological disorders (such asÂ <a title=\"Autoimmune disease\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoimmune_disease\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">autoimmune diseases</span></a>,Â <a title=\"Hypersensitivity\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypersensitivity\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">hypersensitivities</span></a>,Â <a title=\"Immune deficiency\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immune_deficiency\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">immune deficiency</span></a>,Â andÂ <a title=\"Transplant rejection\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transplant_rejection\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">transplant rejection</span></a>); and the physical, chemical, and physiological characteristics of the components of the immune systemÂ <em><a title=\"In vitro\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_vitro\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">in vitro</span></a></em>,</span><sup id=\"cite_ref-8\" style=\"unicode-bidi: isolate;\"></sup><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">Â <em><a title=\"In situ\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_situ#Biology_and_Biomedical_Engineering\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">in situ</span></a></em>, andÂ <em><a title=\"In vivo\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_vivo\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">in vivo</span></a></em>.Â Immunology has applications in numerous disciplines of medicine, particularly in the fields of organ transplantation, oncology, rheumatology, virology, bacteriology, parasitology, psychiatry, and dermatology.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; background: white; line-height: inherit; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; word-spacing: 0px; margin: 6pt 0cm;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">The term was coined by Russian biologistÂ <a title=\"Ilya Ilyich Mechnikov\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilya_Ilyich_Mechnikov\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">Ilya Ilyich Mechnikov</span></a>,Â who advanced studies on immunology and received the Nobel Prize for his work in 1908. He pinned small thorns into starfish larvae and noticed unusual cells surrounding the thorns. This was the active response of the body trying to maintain its integrity. It was Mechnikov who first observed the phenomenon ofÂ <a title=\"Phagocytosis\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phagocytosis\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">phagocytosis</span></a>Â in which the body defends itself against a foreign body.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; background: white; line-height: inherit; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; word-spacing: 0px; margin: 6pt 0cm;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">Prior to the designation ofÂ <a title=\"Immunity (medical)\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immunity_(medical)\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">immunity</span></a>Â from the etymological rootÂ <em>immunis</em>, which isÂ <a title=\"Latin\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latin\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">Latin</span></a>Â for \"exempt\", early physicians characterized organs that would later be proven as essential components of the immune system. The important lymphoid organs of the immune system are theÂ <a title=\"Thymus\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thymus\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">thymus</span></a>,</span><sup id=\"cite_ref-13\" style=\"unicode-bidi: isolate;\"><span style=\"font-size: 8.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immunology#cite_note-13\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">[13]</span></a></span></sup><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">Â <a title=\"Bone marrow\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_marrow\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">bone marrow</span></a>, and chief lymphatic tissues such asÂ <a title=\"Spleen\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spleen\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">spleen</span></a>,Â <a title=\"Tonsil\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonsil\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">tonsils</span></a>,Â <a title=\"Lymphatic system\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lymphatic_system\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">lymph vessels</span></a>,Â <a title=\"Lymph node\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lymph_node\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">lymph nodes</span></a>,Â <a title=\"Adenoid\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adenoid\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">adenoids</span></a>, andÂ <a title=\"Liver\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liver\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">liver</span></a>. When health conditions worsen to emergency status, portions of immune system organs, including the thymus, spleen, bone marrow, lymph nodes, and other lymphatic tissues, can beÂ <a title=\"Surgery\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surgery\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">surgically</span></a>Â excised for examination while patients are still alive.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; background: white; line-height: inherit; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; word-spacing: 0px; margin: 6pt 0cm;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \'Arial\',\'sans-serif\';\">Many components of the immune system are typicallyÂ <a title=\"Cell (biology)\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cell_(biology)\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">cellular</span></a>Â in nature and not associated with any specific organ, but rather are embedded or circulating in variousÂ <a title=\"Tissue (biology)\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tissue_(biology)\"><span style=\"color: windowtext; text-decoration: none; text-underline: none;\">tissues</span></a>Â located throughout the body.</span></p>', '', 'e67b9b54c96a3291bf3b909fa339de03.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 19:12:48', '2019-08-25 19:44:13', 1, '2019-08-25 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(137, 64, 0, 'Latex Agglutination Kits', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Latex Agglutination Kits</strong>, these tests depend on the agglutination of antibody coated latex particles with antigens from corresponding microorganisms from various sources such as biological fluids from patients, liquid broth media etc. These Latex Agglutination tests are extremely rapid (typically less than 15 minutes) and simple to perform, can be read by eye and do not require expensive equipment. Moreover the reagents are stable in the refrigerator (2-8 C) for 13 months. These tests also have very high sensitivity and specificity, making them an excellent choice for a variety of broad applications such as rapid screening of multiple samples for infection, microbial contamination or microbial identification.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>For inquiry please kindly email to : lisa@prolabios.com</strong></p>', '', '32bd855024647cc5384c32a6e642d964.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 19:57:53', '2020-03-08 20:23:24', 1, '2020-03-08 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(138, 65, 0, 'Chemical Indicator', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Chemical Indicator</strong> strips and challenge packs capture sterilization or disinfection failures through immediate results, while external indicator tapes and labels provide confirmation that a pack has been exposed to the sterilization process and helps distinguish between processed and unprocessed packs.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>For inquiry please kindly email to : lisa@prolabios.com</strong></p>', '', 'dd2843472bfe0c4545abd5bfd0aa1ccd.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 20:17:42', '2020-03-08 20:23:05', 1, '2020-03-08 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `web_content` (`content_id`, `channel_id`, `content_cat_id`, `title`, `title_eng`, `description`, `description_eng`, `file`, `file_eng`, `posted`, `updated`, `status`, `published`, `type`, `param1`, `param2`, `param3`, `ispromo`) VALUES
(139, 66, 0, 'MIC Test Strip for antimicrobial susceptibility testing', '', '<p><strong>Quantitative assay for determining the Minimum Inhibitory Concentration (M.I.C.)</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Â </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>MIC Test Strip</strong> is a quantitative assay for determining the Minimum Inhibitory Concentration (M.I.C.) of antimicrobial agents against microorganisms and for detecting the resistance mechanisms. MIC Test Strip are porous strips with special features <strong>(International Patent)</strong> that are impregnated with a predefined concentration gradient of antibiotic, across 15 two-fold dilutions of a conventional M.I.C. method.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On one side of the strip is indicated a M.I.C. scale in Î¼g/mL and a code that identify the antimicrobial agent. For ESBL, MBL, GRD, AmpC and KPC detection, the double-sided gradient carries the appropriate diagnostic reagents. MIC Test Strip are available in a large variety of configurations. Each configuration is available in packages of 10, 30 and 100 tests.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Method Principle</strong><br />When the MIC Test Strip is applied onto an inoculated agar surface, the preformed exponential gradient of antimicrobial agent is immediately transferred to the agar matrix. After 18 hours incubation or longer, a symmetrical inhibition ellipse centered along the strip is formed. The MIC is read directly from the scale in terms of Î¼g/mL at the point where the edge of the inhibition ellipse intersects the strip MIC Test Strip. Other growth/inhibition patterns may also be seen for resistance detection methods.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Â </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>BIBLIOGRAPHY</strong><br />â€¢ CLSI M100-S26 , 2016. Performance Standards for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing.<br />â€¢ CLSI M7-A10, 2015. Methods for Dilution Antimicrobial Susceptibility Tests for Bacteria that Grow Aerobically.<br />â€¢ CLSI M11-A8 Methods for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing of Anaerobic Bacteria.<br />â€¢ CLSI M11-S1 Performance Standards for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing of Anaerobic Bacteria.<br />â€¢ CLSI M27-A3. Reference Method for Broth Dilution Antifungal Susceptibility Testing of Yeasts; Approved Standard - Third Edition.<br />â€¢ CLSI M27-S4. Reference Method for Broth Dilution Antifungal Susceptibility Testing of Yeasts; Fourth Informational supplement.<br />â€¢ EUCAST. Breakpoint tables for interpretation of MICs and zone diameters Version 6.0 , January 2016.</p>', '', 'df7425ad8dc74957c4dd7c67c7bcd2dc.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 20:30:33', '2019-09-09 22:23:11', 1, '2019-09-09 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(86, 5, 0, 'Kinerja Kuartal III/2016 : Pemakaian Air PerRumah Tangga di Jakarta Stabil', 'Performance Quarter III / 2016: Water Usage Per Household in Jakarta Stable', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Konsumsi air minum pelanggan di Jakarta pada kuartal III 2016 relatif stabil. Hasil evaluasi BRPAM terhadap pola konsumsi pelanggan air minum Jakarta hingga &nbsp;kuartal III memperlihatkan bahwa pola penggunaan air setiap bulan memiliki kecenderungan sama dengan pola konsumsi perbulan tahun 2015. Pada kuartal III, &nbsp;konsumsi rata-rata pelanggan adalah 33,14 m3/pelanggan/bulan. Jumlah ini menurun sedikit dibanding rata-rata pemakaian tahun 2015, yang berjumlah 33,55m3/pelanggan/bulan. Pada awal kuartal 3, yaitu bulan Juli dan Agustus 2016 konsumsinya mencapai 32,09 m3/pelanggan dan 32,27 m3/pelanggan, dan berada dibawah rata-rata pemakaian tahun 2015.. Bila dibandingkan kondisi perbulan hingga kuartal 3, pemakain tertinggi terjadi pada bulan Juni 2016, yaitu sebesar 35,37m3/ pelanggan/ bulan.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Pola konsumsi pelanggan air minum di Jakarta, hingga September tahun 2016 ditampilkan pada gambar berikut.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;<img title=\"Keterangan Gambar\" src=\"/content/photo/5a58049f7ee661deaa6dcbfb6d8fd82a.jpg\" alt=\". Konsumsi Rata-Rata Jakarta Januari - September 2016\" width=\"489\" height=\"319\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />Konsumsi air rata-rata pelanggan wilayah Barat (dilayani oleh Palyja) mencapai 33,01 m3/pelanggan/bulan, dan angka ini dibawah pemakaian rata-rata pelanggan &nbsp;Palyja pada tahun 2015,yang sebesar adalah 32,99 m3/plg/bln. Pada wilayah Timur (dilayani oleh Aetra) konsumsi air rata-rata mencapai 33,26 m3/pelanggan/bln, &nbsp;dimana angka ini lebih rendah dari pemakaian rata-rata pelanggan Aetra pada tahun 2015 yang mencapai 34,10 m3/pelanggan/bln</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BRPAM juga melalukan evaluasi terhadap pemakaian minimum pelanggan, dan menenukan adanya pelanggan dengan pemakaian 0 (nol) m3/bulan.<br /> <br />Jumlah pelanggan dengan pemakaian 0 m3 (pelanggan nol kubik) pada wilayah Barat meningkat.. Dibanding kondisi awal 2016, pada September 2016 jumlah pelanggan nol kubik naik sebesar 1,42%. Untuk wilayah Timur mengalami kenaikan sebesar 0,45%. Jumlah pelanggan nol kubik di wilayah Barat lebih banyak dibanding wilaya Timur.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hasil diskusi BRPAM dengan operator air minum di kedua wilayah mencatat bahwa pelanggan nol kubik umumnya terjadi akibat alasan (i)pelanggan memiliki sumber lain selain PDAM (misalnya sumur) dan atau (ii) pelanggan yang memang tidak mendapatkan pelayanan yang baik dari operator karena tekanan yang tidak memadai. Terhadap pelanggan nol kubik ini, BRPAM telah menyurati operator dan mendiskusikannya agar diambil langkah-langkah yang progresif dan konstruktif untuk mengatasi masalah pelanggan dan mendorong mereka menjadi pelanggan yang bukan nol kubik.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sebagaimana diketahui, dalamPerjanjianKerjasama PAM Jaya dengan Palyja dan Aetra, terdapat 5 parameter target teknis ditetapkan sebagai indikator kinerja. Parameter tersebut adalah Jumlah Sambungan, Produksi Air, Cakupan Pelayanan, Volume Air Terjual dan Tingkat Kehilangan Air. Kelima parameter mengacu pada Rebasing PAM Jaya dan PALYJA, dan Master Agreement PAM Jaya dan Aetra. Penilaian pencapaian target teknis setiap parameter, dilakukan pada 2 wilayah pelayanan, yaitu wilayah Barat untuk yang dilayani PALYJA dan wilayah Timur dilayani oleh Aetra. Laporan lengkap Kinerja Q3 dapat menghubungi sekretariat BRPAM, klik <a href=\"/contact-us/\">Kontak Kami</a>&nbsp;(#SK/dhs).</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Consumption of drinking water customer in the third quarter of 2016 was relatively stable. The evaluation results BRPAM against customer consumption patterns of drinking water to Jakarta the third quarter showed that the pattern of water usage each month has a tendency similar to the pattern of consumption per month in 2015. In the third quarter, the average consumption of customers is 33.14 m3 / customer / month. This number decreased slightly compared to the average consumption in 2015, which amounted 33,55m3 /customer / month. At the beginning of the 3rd quarter, ie July and August 2016 consumption reached 32.09 m3 / subscribers and 32.27 m3 / customer, and under Average consumption in 2015 .. When compared condition per month until the 3rd quarter, the highest usage occurred in June 2016, which amounted 35,37m3 / customer / month.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Customer consumption patterns of drinking water in Jakarta, until September 2016 is shown in the following picture.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img title=\"Average consumption Jakarta from January to September - 2016\" src=\"/content/photo/5a58049f7ee661deaa6dcbfb6d8fd82a.jpg\" alt=\"Average consumption Jakarta from January to September - 2016\" width=\"489\" height=\"319\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />The average water consumption of the West region customers (served by Palyja) reached 33.01 m3 / customer / month, and this figure is below the average customer usage Palyja in 2015, which amounted was 32.99 m3 / PLG / mo. In the Eastern region (served by Aetra) water consumption reached an average of 33.26 m3 / customer / month, where this figure is lower than the average customer usage Aetra in 2015 which reached 34.10 m3 / customer / month</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BRPAM also put through an evaluation of the minimum usage customers, and their customers with user menenukan 0 (zero) m3 / month.<br />&nbsp;<br />The number of customers with the use of 0 m3 (cubic zero customers) in the Western region increased .. Compared to the initial conditions in 2016, in September 2016 the number of subscribers zero cubic rose by 1.42%. For East region increased by 0.45%. The number of customers cubic zero in the West more than East wilaya.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Results BRPAM discussions with operators of drinking water in the region noted that zero customers cubic mainly due to the reason (i) the customer has other sources besides taps (eg wells) or (ii) customers who did not get good service from the carrier because the pressure is not adequate. To This cubic zero customers, BRPAM has written to the operator and to discuss the steps to be taken are progressive and constructive to resolve the problem customers and encouraging them to become customers instead of zero cubic.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As known, dalamPerjanjianKerjasama PAM Jaya and Palyja and Aetra, there are five parameters technical targets set as a performance indicator. Parameter is Number Dialling, Water Production, Scope of Services, Air Volume Sold and Water Loss Rate. The fifth parameter refers to the rebasing PAM Jaya and PALYJA, and the Master Agreement PAM Jaya and Aetra. Ratings achievement of technical targets of each parameter, performed on two service areas, namely the West to served PALYJA and East regions served by Aetra. The full report can contact the secretariat Q3 performance BRPAM, Click Contact<a href=\"/contact-us/\">&nbsp;</a>Us. (# SK / dhs).&nbsp;</p>', 'ea422459a8d4d8b9fab230231336a6cc.jpg', '', '2016-11-21 21:30:22', '2016-11-21 21:43:03', 3, '2016-11-21 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(96, 19, 0, 'Struktur Organisasi Badan Regulator Pelayanan Air Minum DKI Jakarta (BRPAM)', 'Organization Structure Jakarta Water Supply Regulatory Body (JWSRB)', '<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/content/photo/9a7a71122167cae358808ca15a0cbe32.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"558\" height=\"451\" /></p>', '<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/content/photo/9a7a71122167cae358808ca15a0cbe32.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"558\" height=\"451\" /></p>', '', '', '2016-12-05 21:03:49', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 3, '2016-12-05 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(151, 37, 0, 'Biomolecular', '', '<p><strong>Biomolecular</strong> is the application of principles and practices to the purposeful manipulation of molecules of biological origin. Biomolecular engineers integrate knowledge of biological processes with the core knowledge of chemical engineering in order to focus on molecular level solutions to issues and problems in the life sciences related to the environment, agriculture, energy, industry, food production, biotechnology and medicine.</p>\r\n<p>Biomolecular engineers purposefully manipulate carbohydrates, proteins, nucleic acids and lipids within the framework of the relation between their structure (see: nucleic acid structure, carbohydrate chemistry, protein structure,), function (see: protein function) and properties and in relation to applicability to such areas as environmental remediation, crop and livestock production, biofuel cells and biomolecular diagnostics. The thermodynamics and kinetics of molecular recognition in enzymes, antibodies, DNA hybridization, bio-conjugation/bio-immobilization and bioseparations are studied. Attention is also given to the rudiments of engineered biomolecules in cell signaling, cell growth kinetics, biochemical pathway engineering and bioreactor engineering.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Culture media &amp; reagent for biomolecular</strong></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.359%; height: 147px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 29px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; height: 29px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Catalogue</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 29px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Product</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 29px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Application</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; height: 10px; text-align: center;\">610028</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 10px;\">MacConkey Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 10px; text-align: left;\">Selective and differential medium for detection of Enterobacteriaceae from clinical samples and other materials, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610245</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 18px;\">LB Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for the cultivation of <em>Escherichia coli</em> used in molecular genetic studies.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610084</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 18px;\">LB Medium (LURIA BERTANI)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Dehydrated medium for maintaining and cultivating of recombinant strains of <em>Escherichia coli.</em></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610337</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 18px;\">MacConkey Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Liquid enrichment medium for detection of coliform bacteria, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610171</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 18px;\">MacConkey Broth (Purple)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Selective medium for coliform detection in water and milk.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610149</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 18px;\">MacConkey Broth MODIFIED (w/o NaCl)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Selective medium for coliform detection in water and milk.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8543%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610170</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 30.4428%; height: 18px;\">MacConkey MUG Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.5522%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Selective medium for <em>Escherichia coli</em> isolation from lactose non-fermenting bacteria.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '', '701814347d8fbcead4ddbaa55b3cad8f.jpg', '', '2019-09-09 22:17:42', '2019-10-18 15:47:36', 1, '2019-10-18 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(153, 38, 0, 'Clinical', '', '<p><strong>Clinical microbiology</strong> is the study of micro organisms that caused infections and diseases to Human and other animals. It is an adaptation of microbiological techniques to the study of etiological agents of infectious disease. It often deals with hospital-acquired and public-health problems that affect both hospital and community. It is related to the laboratory diagnosis of human and animal infections and the role of the laboratory in both the management of infectious diseases and the elucidation of the epidemiology of infections. The latest developments in clinical microbiology and immunology, providing the current state of knowledge in the field, as well as balanced, thought-provoking perspectives on controversial issues.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Culture media & reagent for clinical analysis</strong></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 95.6887%; height: 2149px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 23.3029%; height: 28px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Parameter</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.48152%; height: 28px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Catalogue</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 41.2497%; height: 28px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Product</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 23.3029%; height: 126px; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"7\"><strong>Aerobic Microorganism Plate Count</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.48152%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">611402</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 41.2497%; height: 18px;\">CARY BLAIR Transport Medium</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.48152%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610036</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 41.2497%; height: 18px;\">Nutrient Agar</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 7.48152%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610040</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 41.2497%; height: 18px;\">Plate 