\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">RAPPAPORT VASSILIADIS Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 54px;\">Enrichment medium for <em>Salmonella spp</em> isolation from meat and dairy products, feces and sewage polluted water, according to ISO 6579 and ISO 6785.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610178</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Rose Bengal Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Basal medium for the selective isolation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610090</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Rose Bengal CAF Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for detection of yeasts and moulds from food and environmental materials.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610103</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">Sabouraud Dextrose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 54px;\">Medium for the cultivation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds<br />from different materials, according to EN ISO 11133 and USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610104</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Sabouraud Dextrose Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium for the cultivation of yeasts and moulds from different materials, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610203</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Sabouraud CAF Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for the cultivation and isolation of pathogenic and nonpathogenic fungi.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610179</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Sabouraud CAF Agar + Actidione</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for isolation and cultivation of pathogenic fungi from clinical specimens.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610146</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">Sabouraud Maltose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Medium for pathogenic and saprophytic fungi isolation.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610145</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Selenite Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium for selective enrichment of Salmonella spp, from clinical and nonclinical samples, according to APHA.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610150</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Selenite CYSTINE Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium for detection of <em>Salmonella spp</em> according to ISO 6785.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610181</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">SIM Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for indole, motility and H2S tests.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610046</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">SIMMONS CITRATE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for enterobacteria identification.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610134</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">SLANETZ AND BARTLEY Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for detection and enumeration of enterococci in water and other materials, according to ISO 7899-2.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610147</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">SLANETZ AND BARTLEY Agar + TTC</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 54px;\">Selective medium for fecal streptococci enumeration and isolation, according to the formulation reported by ISO 7899-2:2000.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610224</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">T.B.X. Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Chromogenic medium for detection and enumeration of <em>E. coli</em>,<br />according to ISO 16649 (all parts).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">611010</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">T.C.B.S. Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for detection of enteropathogenic <em>Vibrio spp</em><br />from clinical and nonclinical samples, according to ISO 21872.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610055</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">T.S.I. Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for enterobacteria identification.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610183</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">TETRATHIONATE Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Enrichment medium for isolating <em>Salmonella typhi</em> and other salmonellae from feces, sewage, etc.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610052</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">Tryptic Soy Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 54px;\">General purpose medium for the cultivation of a wide variety of organisms from clinical and nonclinical specimens, according to EN ISO 11133.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610053</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Tryptic Soy Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium for the isolation and cultivation of a wide variety of organisms, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610206</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">Tryptone Water</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for detection of <em>E. coli </em>in clinical specimens, food and water samples, according to ISO 7251and ISO 3811.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610197</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">Tryptophan Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Dehydrated medium for the production of indole by microrganisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610107</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">UREA Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Medium for urease test, recommended by ISO 6785 and IDF 93.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610311</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">UREA Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for detection of urea-utilizing organisms from clinical and nonclinical samples.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610187</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Violet Red Bile Agar MUG</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Medium for the detection of <em>Escherichia coli</em> and total coliform in water, food and dairy products.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610059</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Violet Red Bile Glucose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for detection and enumeration of Enterobacteriaceae in food, water and other materials, according to USP/EP/JP and ISO 21528.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610058</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Violet Red Bile Lactose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Violet Red Bile Agar Vegitone is a selective media used for the detection and enumeration of coliform organisms from water and food. This medium contains no animal derived peptone and bile salt</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610382</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Water Detect COLIFORMS</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Chromogenic medium for detection of <em>E. coli</em> and other coliforms in water.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610060</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">XLD Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for detection of <em>Salmonella</em> and <em>Shigella spp</em> in food, environmental samples and other materials, according to ISO 6579 and ISO 21567.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610092</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">XLT 4 Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for non-typhi Salmonella isolation.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">611016</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Yeast Extract Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Nutrient medium for the enumeration of microorganisms in water and materials of sanitary importance, according to ISO 6222.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610070</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Yeast Glucose Chloramphenicol Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for the isolation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds in foodstuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610369</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Yersinia ITC BROTH BASE</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Selective liquid medium for detection of <em>Yersinia enterocolitica</em>, according to ISO 10273.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610370</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">Yersinia PSB Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Selective liquid medium for detection of <em>Yersinia enterocolitica</em>, according to ISO 10273.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610111</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 29.1417%;\" width=\"584\">YERSINIA SELECTIVE Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.3273%; height: 18px;\">Differential and selective medium for the isolation of <em>Y. enterocolitica</em> from clinical and nonclinical specimens, according to ISO 10273.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '', 'c7f8446d7988aecec6ee28c5191621d6.jpg', '', '2019-09-09 23:09:48', '2019-10-18 15:24:53', 1, '2019-10-18 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `web_content` (`content_id`, `channel_id`, `content_cat_id`, `title`, `title_eng`, `description`, `description_eng`, `file`, `file_eng`, `posted`, `updated`, `status`, `published`, `type`, `param1`, `param2`, `param3`, `ispromo`) VALUES
(165, 41, 0, 'Food', '', '<p>Our principal has a strong heritage of providing high quality food safety solutions, supporting the whole food and beverage production chain through from manufacture to the food safety testing laboratories.</p>\r\n<p>Products designed for use within food safety testing are primarily concerned with three areas: core pathogens, spoilage organisms and indicator organisms. Our principal has a long standing and industry trusted catalogue of traditional microbiology products as well as an expanding range of innovative solutions for rapid testing.</p>\r\n<p>We can offer products to meet the requirements of any testing protocol, from specified ISO workflows through to alternative methods. We has been working with food and beverage manufacturers and testing laboratories who specialise in food safety analysis for many years and has a wealth of experience and knowledge to support you in managing risk and improving food safety.</p>\r\n<p>Culture media &amp; reagent for Food analysis</p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 1035px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 27px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 27px;\"><strong>Catalogue</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; text-align: center; height: 27px;\"><strong>Product&nbsp;</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: center; height: 27px;\"><strong>Application</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610105</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">A1 Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Basal medium for Fecal coliforms detection in water.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610312</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">ACETAMIDE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Dehydrated medium for the differentiation of nonfermentative gram-negative bacteria, particularly <em>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</em>.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610313</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">ACETAMIDE Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Dehydrated medium for the confirmation test of <em>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</em> in bottled water.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610392</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Acetamide Broth ISO 16266</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for detection of <em>P. aeruginosa</em> in water samples, according to ISO 16266.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610098</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">ALKALINE Peptone Water</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Enrichment medium for Vibrio spp. isolation from drinks, foods or sewage.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610300</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">APT Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Medium for the cultivation and enumeration of heterofermentative lactobacilli</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610153</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">Azide Blood Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 36px;\">A selective medium for the detection and isolation of Streptococci and Staphylococci from stool, sewage, food and other specimens.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610003</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Azide Dextrose Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for fecal streptococci detection and enumeration in waters and foodstuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610154</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Azide Maltose Agar KF</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for fecal streptococci detection and enumeration in waters and foodstuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610155</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Azide VIOLET Blood Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Selective basal medium for streptococci isolation from clinical samples and foodstuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610114</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">BACILLUS CEREUS Agar Base (MOSSEL, MYP)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Basal medium for the isolation and enumeration of <em>Bacillus cereus</em>, according to ISO 7932, ISO 21871 and FDA-BAM.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610136</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">BACILLUS CEREUS Agar Base (PEMBA)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for <em>Bacillus cereus</em> isolation and enumeration in foodstuffs.<!-- )&2) 41$ )8;\r\n&\'1.&.$*=28 )86 $;$4;:(1286 )=; 91<(-.*=;W X$ Z[ ]^[Z_ E`aMbcM d \'&(135-,; )$ ,01</ <$0013(4&1$6K G^_Z\r\nLghiB jhkGlmn_--></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610004</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Baird Parker Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">For the isolation and differentiation of&nbsp;<em>Staphylococci&nbsp;</em>in food and pharmaceuticals according to Baird-Parker.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610361</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">BAT Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 36px;\">Medium for detection of <em>Alicyclobacillus spp</em> in fruit juices and other beverages.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610210</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Bile Aesculin Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for group <em>D streptococci</em> isolation in foods and pharmaceutical products.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610151</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Bile Aesculin Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Sellective medium for group <em>D streptococci</em> isolation in foods and pharmaceutical products.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610001</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">Bile Aesculin Azide Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for detection and enumeration of enterococci in water and other materials, according to ISO 7899-2.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610157</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">BIOTONE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Medium for fastidious microorganisms, including <em>Brucella spp.</em>, cultivation and maintenance.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610301</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">BISMUTH Sulfite Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Dehydrated medium for the isolation and differentation of <em>Salmonella</em> <em>typhi</em> and other salmonellae.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610005</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Blood Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px;\">Non-selective medium for the isolation and cultivation of many pathogenic and non-pathogenic microorganisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610188</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Blood Agar Base No.2</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Formulated to yield maximum recovery of fastidious pathogenic microorganisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610009</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Brilliant Green Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">A highly selective medium for the isolation and identification of Salmonella except S. typhosa or Shigella species.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610010</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Brilliant Green Bile Broth 2%</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">For the selective enrichment and enumeration by titer determination or MPN method of&nbsp;<em>E. coli</em>&nbsp;and other fecal coliform from water, milk, food and other material.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610079</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Brucella Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Recommended for enrichment, isolation and cultivation of&nbsp;<em>Brucella</em>&nbsp;species.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610142</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">BRYANT AND BURKEY Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Bryant and Burkey Medium is used for detecting and enumerating spores of lactate fermenting Clostridium in milk and dairy products.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 108px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 108px;\">611014</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 108px;\">Buffered Peptone Water</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 108px;\">Liquid medium recommended by ISO 6579 for increasing the recovery of injured Salmonella spp. from food and associated samples prior to selective enrichment and isolation. According to ISO 21528, Buffered Peptone Water is used for detection or enumeration of Enterobacteriaceae within foodstuffs. Used as diluent, Buffered Peptone Water complies with ISO 6887 and 11290 for the enumeration of organisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">611007</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Campylobacter Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">For the isolation of Campylobacter species from human and animal derived clinical material, and from contaminated food, water etc.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">611007</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Campylobacter Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Used for selective isolation and differentiation of Campylobacter species.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610130</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Campylobacter Blood FREE Medium Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Used for selective isolation and differentiation of&nbsp;<em>Campylobacter</em>&nbsp;species.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610131</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Campylobacter ENRICHMENT Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Used for selective isolation and differentiation of&nbsp;<em>Campylobacter</em>&nbsp;species.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610200</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Campylobacter KARMALI Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Used for selective isolation and differentiation of&nbsp;<em>Campylobacter</em>&nbsp;species.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610041</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">CETRIMIDE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">For the isolation and differentiation of&nbsp;<em>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</em> from different material.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610362</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">CHINA-BLUE Lactose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Selective medium for differentiating lactose fermenting and lactose non-fermenting microorganisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610628</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Chromatic&trade; Bacillus cereus</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Chromogenic medium for detection of <em>Bacillus cereus</em> in food and environmental samples.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610390</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Chromatic&trade; Cronobacter Isolation Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">chromogenic medium used for the isolation of <em>Cronobacter spp.</em> (formerly Enterobacter sakazakii) from food, animal feed and environmental samples in areas of food production and handling. According to ISO 22964:2017, CCI is used in conjunction with Cronobacter Selective Broth (CSB).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610630</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Chromatic&trade; Coliform Agar ISO</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Chromogenic medium for detection and enumeration of <em>E. coli</em> and coliform bacteria in water, according to ISO 9308-1.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610610</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Chromatic&trade; Coli/Coliform</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Chromogenic medium for detection and enumeration of <em>Escherichia coli</em> and coliform bacteria in food and water.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610601</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">O.A. Listeria Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Chromogenic selective medium for <em>Listeria monocytogenes</em> isolation and differentiation (ISO 11290).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610611</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Chromatic&trade; Salmonella</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Chromogenic selective medium for isolation and differentiation of <em>Salmonella</em> <em>spp.</em> (including <em>S. typhi</em>).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610616</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Chromatic&trade; Staph aureus</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Chromogenic medium for the isolation and differentiation of <em>Staphylococcus</em> <em>aureus</em> directly from clinical and nonclinical specimens.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610224</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">TBX Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Chromogenic medium for detection and enumeration of <em>E. coli,</em> according to ISO 16649 (all parts).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610056</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Clostridium Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Medium for the cultivation and the enumeration of clostridia and other anaerobes from foods and clinical samples.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610207</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Clostridium Perfringens Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Basal medium for detection of C. perfringens from clinical specimens and other materials according to ISO 7937 and ISO 14189.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 90px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 90px;\" width=\"64\">610372</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 90px;\">Cooked Meat Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 90px; text-align: justify;\">Medium for the cultivation and maintenance of anaerobic organisms, especially pathogenic clostridia, differentiating saccharolytic from proteolytic species. This medium permits growth from a small inoculum, important for clinical specimens. It is also recommended in standard methods for food testing for the enumeration and identification of Clostridium perfringens.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610389</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Cronobacter Selective Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Selective liquid medium for detection of <em>Cronobacter spp</em>, according to ISO 22964:2017.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610091</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Demi Fraser Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Medium for primary enrichment of <em>Listeria spp.</em> according ISO 11290.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610198</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Dextrose Tryptone Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Medium for cultivating thermophilic &ldquo;flat sour&rdquo; microorganisms from food spoilage.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610238</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Dichloran-Glycerol (DG18) Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Selective medium for the enumeration of yeasts and moulds, according to ISO 21527-2:2008.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610237</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Dichloran Rose-Bengal Chloramphenicol Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Selective medium for the enumeration of yeasts and moulds, according to ISO 21527-1:2008.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610063</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">E.C. Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Selective liquid medium for detection and enumeration of coliform bacteria and <em>E. coli</em> in water and food, according to ISO 7251.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">610332</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">E.C. Broth MUG</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 36px;\">Selective broth for fecal coliforms and E. coli detection in water, wastewater, shellfish and foods.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610017</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">E.E. Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for the cultivation and selective enrichment of Enterobacteriaceae from different types of samples, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610019</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">E.M.B. LEVINE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for gram-negative enteric bacteria isolation (harmonized US Pharmacopeia)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610020</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">ENDO Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for coliforms confirmatory test.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610623</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Enterobacter (Cronobacter) sakazakii Isolation Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; height: 18px; text-align: justify;\">Enterobacter (Cronobacter) sakazakii Isolation Agar is a chromogenic medium used for the selective isolation of<br />Cronobacter spp (formerly E. sakazakii) in infant milk products, according to ISO 22964:2006.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610375</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Fraser Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Enrichment medium for detection and enumeration of Listeria monocytogenes and Listeria spp, according to ISO 11290 (both parts).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610054</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Gelatin Peptone Agar (Agar gelisato)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for the cultivation of non-fastidious organisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610100</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Giolitti Cantoni Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Basal medium for <em>Staphylococcus aureus</em> enrichment from foods, recommended by ISO 6888-3: 2003</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610388</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Glucose OF Medium ISO 21528</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Glucose OF medium is a semisoild medium used for the identification of gram-negative bacteria on the basis of their ability to oxidize or ferment glucose. This medium complies with ISO 21528:2017 for confirmation of Enterobacteriaceae from food, animal feeding stuffs and environmental samples.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">611021</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Heart Infusion Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Heart Infusion Broth is used for general laboratory purpose for the cultivation of fastidious organisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610021</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Hektoen Enteric Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective and differential medium for detection of pathogenic intestinal bacteria from food and clinical specimens, according to ISO 21567.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610190</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Kanamycin Aesculin Azide Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for isolation of enterococci in foods and foodstuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">611202</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Lactose Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Recommended for use in the presumptive test for members of the coliform group in water, milk and other material. It corresponds largely to the formulation of the United States Pharmacopoeia.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610360</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Lactose GELATIN Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Dehydrated medium for the identification of <em>C. perfringens</em> by lactose and gelatin test (ISO 7937).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610358</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Lactose Sulfite Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for detection of <em>C. perfringens</em>, according to EP and ISO 7937.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610247</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Lauryl Sulfate Tryptose Broth Modified (m-LST)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective liquid medium for detection of <em>Cronobacter spp</em>, according to ISO 22964:2006.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610085</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">LAURYL TRYPTOSE Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium acc. to Mallmann and Darby (1941) for the presumptive testing for coliform and their selective enrichment in the examination of water, dairy products and food.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610326</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Listeria Enrichment Broth Base (Lovett)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Broth for enrichment of Listeria spp. according to Lovett\'s formulation.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610166</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Listeria FRASER Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for secondary enrichment of <em>Listeria spp</em>.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610167</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Listeria Oxford Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for <em>Listeria spp</em> isolation and differentiation in foods, milk and dairy products and clinical and environmental samples (ISO 10560:1993).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610231</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Listeria Oxford Agar Base ISO 11290</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Basal medium without antibiotics and acriflavine for the isolation of <em>Listeria monocytogenes</em> according to ISO 11290.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610168</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Listeria PALCAM Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for the isolation and enumeration of <em>Listeria monocytogenes</em> according to ISO 11290-1.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610031</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Listeria UVM 1 Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for <em>Listeria spp</em> enrichment.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610045</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Listeria UVM 2 Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for <em>Listeria spp</em> enrichment.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610318</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">LITMUS MILK</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Litmus milk is used for the maintenance of lactic acid bacteria and as a differential medium for determining the action of bacteria on milk.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610303</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Lysine DECARBOXYLASE Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Dehydrated medium used for identification of microorganisms, especially enteric bacilli, based on the decarboxylation of lysine</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610027</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Lysine IRON Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for enterobacteria isolation.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610192</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">M17 Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for selective enumeration of Streptococcus thermophilus and for the improved growth of lactic streptococci and their bacteriophages.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610018</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">M.S.R.V. (Modified Semisolid Rappaport Vassiliadis) Medium Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for detection of motile <em>Salmonella spp</em> in animal faeces and environmental samples, according to ISO 6579.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610337</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">MacConkey Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">A presumptive medium for the detection of the coliform group in water and milk.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610171</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">MacConkey Broth (Purple)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">MacConkey Broth Purple is a differential medium used for the detection of coliforms in water samples and milk examination by MPN technique. It is a modification of the classic medium, where neutral red is replaced by a less aggressive indicator, according European Pharmacopoeia. It is also recommended by ISO Committee under the specification ISO 9308-2:1990.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610172</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Malonate Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Recommended for the differentiation of&nbsp;<em>Enterobacter</em>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<em>Escherichia</em>.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610101</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Malt Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Used for the detection and isolation of yeasts and molds from dairy products and foods.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610173</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Malt Extract Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">A medium for the isolation and enumeration of yeasts and molds.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610069</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Malt Extract Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">A liquid medium for the cultivation of yeasts and molds.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610235</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Mannitol MOTILITY Test Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Semisolid medium used for the detection of motility of Enterobacteriaceae</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610077</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Maximum Recovery Diluent</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Diluent for preparation of food samples for microbiological examination, according to ISO 6887.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610073</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Milk Plate Count Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for the enumeration of microorganisms in milk and dairy products, according to the APHA and ISO 4833.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610396</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Mineral Modified Glutamate Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Liquid selective enrichment medium for the enumeration of <em>Escherichia coli</em>, according to ISO 16649.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610236</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Motility Indole Urea Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium used for differentiating Enterobacteriaceae based on motility, indole production and urease activity</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610371</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Motility Nitrate CP Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">For the identification of <em>Clostridium perfringens</em>, according to ISO 7937.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610132</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Motility TEST Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Dehydrated medium for detection of motility of gram-negative enteric bacilli according to UNI EN ISO 11290-1:2005.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610032</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">MR-VP Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for Gram-negative bacteria differentiation, recommended by ISO 6785: 2001 and IDF 93: 2001.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610024</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">MRS Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">For the enrichment, cultivation and isolation of all species of&nbsp;<em>Lactobacillus</em>&nbsp;from all types of material according to DeMan, Rogosa and Sharpe.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610025</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">MRS Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">For the enrichment and isolation of all species of Lactobacilli from all types of material.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610035</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Muller Kauffmann Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Basal medium for Salmonella selective enrichment from water, foodstuffs and fecal samples.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610239</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Muller Kauffmann TETRATHIONATE Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Basal medium for detection of <em>Salmonella spp</em> from foodstuffs and environmental samples, according to ISO 6579.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610036</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Nutrient Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for cultivating non-fastidious organisms and confirming <em>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</em>, according to ISO 16266.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610037</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Nutrient Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for the cultivation of nonfastidious microorganisms.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610217</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Nutrient Broth no.2</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium recommended for sterility testing of aerobic organisms as well as a base for the enrichment of special media.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610202</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">O.G.Y.E. Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective agar according to Mossel for the identification and enumeration of yeasts and other fungi in foods, clinical specimens etc.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610038</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Peptone Water</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for cultivation of non-fastidious microorganisms and indole testing as recommended by ISO 7251.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610040</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Plate Count Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for the enumeration of bacteria in food, water and other materials, according to APHA and ISO 4833.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">610102</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">POTATO Dextrose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 36px;\">Recommended for the isolation and enumeration of yeasts and molds in dairy products and food.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610071</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Pseudomonas Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for detection and enumeration of <em>Pseudomonas spp</em>, according to ISO 13720, ISO/TS 11059 and ISO 16266.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610175</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">RAPPAPORT VASSILIADIS Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Used as a selective enrichment medium for the isolation of&nbsp;<em>Salmonella&nbsp;</em>species from food and environmental specimens.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610096</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">REINFORCED CLOSTRIDIAL Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for isolation and enumeration of anaerobes and Clostridium spp recommended by ISO 6461/1.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610176</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Rogosa Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective agar for the isolation and enumeration of lactobacilli belonging to the buccal and intestinal flora, as well as from food such as milk and meat.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610178</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Rose Bengal Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">For the selective isolation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds from environmental materials and food stuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610150</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Selenite CYSTINE Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for detection of Salmonella spp according to ISO 6785.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610046</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">SIMMONS CITRATE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for enterobacteria identification.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610055</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">T.S.I. Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for enterobacteria identification.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610052</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Tryptic Soy Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">General purpose medium for the cultivation of a wide variety of organisms from clinical and nonclinical specimens, according to EN ISO 11133.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610053</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Tryptic Soy Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Highly nutrient liquid medium for the general purposes, formulated according to USP, FDA and Eur. Phar.regulations.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610206</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Tryptone Water</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for detection of <em>E. coli</em> in clinical specimens, food and water samples, according to ISO 7251and ISO 3811.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610349</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">TSYE Agar (Tryptic Soy Yeast Extract Agar)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Medium for detection of <em>Listeria spp</em> in food, according to ISO 11290-1.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610241</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Tryptone Soya Yeast Extract Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Liquid culture medium for the confirmation of <em>Listeria monocytogenes</em> according to ISO 11290.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610107</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">UREA Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Medium for urease test, recommended by ISO 6785 and IDF 93.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center;\">610186</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\">Vogel Johnson Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify;\">Selective basal medium for <em>Staphylococcus aureus</em> isolation.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">610187</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">Violet Red Bile Agar MUG</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for isolation and counting coliforms and <em>E. coli</em> in foodstuffs.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610059</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Violet Red Bile Glucose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for detection and enumeration of Enterobacteriaceae in food, water and other materials, according to USP/EP/JP and ISO 21528.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610058</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Violet Red Bile Lactose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for the enumeration of coliforms in food, water and other materials, according to APHA and ISO 4832.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610060</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">XLD Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for detection of <em>Salmonella</em> and <em>Shigella spp</em> in food, environmental samples and other materials, according to ISO 6579 and ISO 21567.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610092</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">XLT 4 Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for non-typhi <em>Salmonella</em> isolation.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 13.5728%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610070</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Yeast Glucose Chloramphenicol Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 59.6806%; text-align: justify; height: 18px;\">Selective agar for the enumeration and isolation of yeasts and molds in dairy products.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '', '1b568bf3209c0c74e3fde09b68a340e2.jpg', '', '2019-09-09 22:47:42', '2019-10-14 17:34:02', 1, '2019-10-14 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0);
INSERT INTO `web_content` (`content_id`, `channel_id`, `content_cat_id`, `title`, `title_eng`, `description`, `description_eng`, `file`, `file_eng`, `posted`, `updated`, `status`, `published`, `type`, `param1`, `param2`, `param3`, `ispromo`) VALUES
(178, 43, 0, 'Pharmaceutical', '', '<p>Due to the high risk of the products produced, the pharmaceutical industry requires absolute vigilance when it comes to hygiene and microbiological safety. Insufficient control measures can lead to microbial contamination of pharmaceutical products which may result in major, costly recalls.</p>\r\n<p>We offers testing solutions for a wide range of requirements within the pharmaceutical sector such as sterility, bioburden, environmental monitoring and determining antimicrobial and preservative effectiveness.</p>\r\n<p>We also offers the full range of media required for microbial testing as specified in Harmonised European Pharmacopeia (USP/EP/JP).</p>\r\n<p>Culture media &amp; reagent for Food analysis</p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 1368px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>Catalogue</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>Product&nbsp;</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>Application</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610314</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">ANTIBIOTIC Agar No.1</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Medium for determining antibiotic potency by the cylinder plates assay technique.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610316</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">ANTIBIOTIC Broth No.3</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium used for the determination potency of antibiotics by the microbial assay technique following the USP specifications.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\">610315</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\">ANTIBIOTIC Agar No.11</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Medium for determining antibiotic potency by the microbiological assay technique.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610338</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Baird Parker Agar Base acc. to E.P.</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Selective basal medium for <em>Staphylococcus aureus</em> isolation according to European Pharmacopoeia.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610135</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">BIGGY (NICKERSON) Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 54px;\">BiGGY Agar (Nickerson Agar) is used for detection, selective isolation, differentiation and presumptive identification of <em>Candida albicans</em> and <em>Candida tropicalis.</em></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610009</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Brilliant Green Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for isolation of <em>salmonellae</em> from clinical specimens and other materials of sanitary importance.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610335</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\">Buffered NaCl Peptone Solution pH 7.0</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Diluent for detection and enumeration of microorganisms according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610041</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">CETRIMIDE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for <em>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</em> isolation, according to European Pharmaacopoeia.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center;\" width=\"64\">610013</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%;\" width=\"584\">Columbia Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%;\">Medium for fastidious microorganisms isolation from clinicsl samples.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610088</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">D/E Neutralizing Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Liquid medium for testing antiseptics and disinfectants.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610017</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">E.E. Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 54px;\">Liquid medium for the cultivation and selective enrichment of<br />Enterobacteriaceae from different types of samples, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610019</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">E.M.B. LEVINE Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for gram-negative enteric bacteria isolation (harmonized US Pharmacopeia).</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610388</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Glucose OF Medium ISO 21528</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Semisolid medium for determining oxidative or fermentative metabolism of bacteria.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610021</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">Hektoen Enteric Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 54px;\">Selective and differential medium for detection of pathogenic intestinal bacteria from food and clinical specimens, according to ISO 21567.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610023</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">Kligler Iron Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Differential medium for enterobacteria identification.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610076</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Letheen Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Basal medium for coefficient phenol detection of quaternary ammonium disinfectans.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610208</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">Letheen Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Basal medium for coefficient phenol detection of quaternary ammonium disinfectans.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610028</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">MacConkey Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 54px;\">Selective and differential medium for detection of Enterobacteriaceae from clinical samples and other materials, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610171</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">MacConkey Broth (Purple)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for coliform detection in water and milk.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610029</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Mannitol Salt Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for isolation and enumeration of staphylococci<br />from clinical samples and other materials, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">611022</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">MIDDLEBROOK 7 H 10 Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Recommended for isolation, cultivation and sensitivity testing of&nbsp;<em>Mycobacterium</em>.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610036</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Nutrient Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Medium for cultivating non-fastidious organisms and confirming <em>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</em>, according to ISO 16266</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610175</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">RAPPAPORT VASSILIADIS Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 54px;\">Enrichment medium for <em>Salmonella spp</em> isolation from meat and dairy products, feces and sewage polluted water, according to ISO 6579 and ISO 6785.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610096</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">REINFORCED CLOSTRIDIAL Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Medium for detection of clostridia and other anaerobic bacteria from clinical and nonclinical specimens.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610103</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Sabouraud Dextrose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Medium for the cultivation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds<br />from different materials, according to EN ISO 11133 and USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610104</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Sabouraud Dextrose Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium for the cultivation of yeasts and moulds from different materials, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610150</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Selenite CYSTINE Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium for detection of <em>Salmonella spp</em> according to ISO 6785.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610134</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">SLANETZ AND BARTLEY Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Selective medium for detection and enumeration of enterococci in water and other materials, according to ISO 7899-2.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610055</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">T.S.I. Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Differential for enterobacteria identification.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610183</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">TETRATHIONATE Broth Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Enrichment medium for isolating <em>Salmonella typhi</em> and other salmonellae from feces, sewage etc.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610052</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">Tryptic Soy Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 54px;\">General purpose medium for the cultivation of a wide variety of organisms from clinical and nonclinical specimens, according to EN ISO 11133.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 36px;\" width=\"64\">610053</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 36px;\" width=\"584\">Tryptic Soy Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 36px;\">Liquid medium for the isolation and cultivation of a wide variety of organisms, according to USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610059</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">Violet Red Bile Glucose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Selective medium for detection and enumeration of Enterobacteriaceae in food, water and other materials, according to USP/EP/JP and ISO 21528.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610186</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 18px;\" width=\"584\">Vogel Johnson Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 18px;\">Selective basal medium for <em>Staphylococcus aureus</em> isolation.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 54px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.5309%; text-align: center; height: 54px;\" width=\"64\">610060</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 26.7465%; height: 54px;\" width=\"584\">XLD Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 58.7225%; height: 54px;\">Selective medium for detection of <em>Salmonella</em> and <em>Shigella spp</em> in food, environmental samples and other materials, according to ISO 6579 and ISO 21567.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '', 'c9697cc9851edd4480df83674474ced5.jpg', '', '2019-09-09 23:05:10', '2019-10-17 21:26:02', 1, '2019-10-17 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(109, 2, 0, 'PT. Prolabios Mitra Analitika', '', '<h4 class=\"post-body-title\"><em>Our Story</em></h4>\r\n<p><strong>Prolabios Mitra Analitika</strong> <strong>(PMA)</strong> build to be one of distributor in Indonesia with passion on fulfillness the need of product or services as well as the skill and knowledge improvement for common sake. Our success would be the company growth, the&nbsp; employee prosperity and the customers satisfaction.</p>\r\n<h4 class=\"post-body-title\"><em>Our Vision</em></h4>\r\n<p>Being the leading company in need&rsquo;s fulfillment, skill escalation and best partner on finding solution for your needs.</p>\r\n<h4 class=\"post-body-title\"><em>Our Mission</em></h4>\r\n<p><em>Product </em>: To be providers of product and services that is guaranteed for best quality, affordable price and maximum benefit. <em>Users </em>: To be user&rsquo;s partner on product and services understanding, problem solving and actively encourages the skill and knowledge improvement of the personnel for common sake. <em>Purchasing </em>: To be purchasing partner on providing the best quality product, price and services. <em>Aftersales </em>: To be trusted and reliable &lsquo;aftersales services&rsquo; providers</p>\r\n<h4 class=\"post-body-title\">Core Value</h4>\r\n<p><strong>PRO :&nbsp;</strong><strong>P</strong>rofessional,&nbsp;<strong>R</strong>obust,&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>O</strong>ffering the best</p>', '', '59a07289401e6cb58dc0e3077e304943.jpg', '', '2017-11-05 11:51:42', '2024-08-06 20:08:24', 3, '2020-02-03 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 1),
(149, 68, 0, 'Agar Preparator', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BenchTop Agar Sterilizer for increased filling productivity. Short process times of only 60-90 Minutes are achievable due to the new heating system and the inbuilt heat exchanger for fast cool down cycles. Complete system with all components situated in the compact and easy to clean metal housing. The quick lock cover system and transparent safety hood offer easiest operator access. 2 size models for 1-10 and 1-15l ready made Agar available.</p>', '', '1c3955df2cbfbadc834f517887af0d10.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 21:36:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 1, '2019-08-25 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(113, 36, 0, 'Brewing', '', '<p>One of the oldest areas of microbiology, brewing, involves microbial activity at all stages of production. Whilst most of this activity is intentional and required within the brewing process, some pose risk to the quality, wastage and safety of the final product.</p>\r\n<p>Brewing involves microbial activity at every stage, from raw material production and malting to stability in the package. Most of these activities are desirable, as beer is the result of a traditional food fermentation, but others represent threats to the quality of the final product and must be controlled actively through careful management, the daily task of maltsters and brewers globally. This review collates current knowledge relevant to the biology of brewing yeast, fermentation management, and the microbial ecology of beer and brewing.</p>\r\n<p>We offers a wide range of products to enable detection, identification and enumeration of spoilage organisms as well as hygiene markers to effectively manage risk in the brewing industry. Solutions are also available to monitor and manage all of the microbial aspects of fermentation.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Culture media &amp; reagent for brewing analysis</strong></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.536%; height: 280px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>Catalogue</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>Product</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\"><strong>Application</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 10px;\" width=\"64\">610024</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 10px;\">MRS Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 10px; text-align: left;\">Medium for isolation and enumeration of mesophilic lactic acid bacteria, according to 15214.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610025</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">MRS Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for the cultivation of lactobacilli from clinical and non clinical specimens.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610173</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">Malt Extract Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for yeasts and moulds isolation, cultivation and enumeration</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610069</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">Malt Extract Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Liquid medium for the cultivation of yeasts and moulds.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610202</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">O.G.Y.E. Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Selective medium for yeasts and moulds isolation and enumeration in foods and cosmetics.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610078</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">ORANGE SERUM Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for cultivation of microorganisms associated with spoilage of citrus fruit products.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610307</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">ORANGE SERUM Broth</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Broth for cultivation and enumeration of microorganisms associated with spoilage of citrus products.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610040</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">Plate Count Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for the enumeration of bacteria in food, water and other materials, according to APHA and ISO 4833.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610129</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">R2 Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for enumerating heterotrophic organisms in water, according to the EP and APHA.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610334</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">Raka Ray No. 3 Medium</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Basal medium for the selective isolation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610178</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">Rose Bengal Agar Base</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Basal medium for the selective isolation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">610103</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">Sabouraud Dextrose Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for the cultivation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds<br />from different materials, according to EN ISO 11133 and USP/EP/JP.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\" width=\"64\">610234</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">W.L. Nutrient Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Dehydrated medium for cultivating yeasts, molds and bacteria encountered in brewing and industrial fermentation processes.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610323</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">WORT Agar</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Medium for the cultivation, isolation and enumeration of yeasts and moulds.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.32365%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">610080</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 33.3873%; height: 18px;\">WORT Broth w/o NaCl</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.94%; height: 18px; text-align: left;\">Basal medium for isolation and enumeration of yeast and moulds.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '', 'af4979aec82de3244edd5a3fca612bbd.jpg', '', '2018-08-05 14:34:56', '2019-10-18 15:41:20', 1, '2019-10-18 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(114, 3, 0, 'Contact Us', '', '<p><iframe style=\"border: 0;\" src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m14!1m8!1m3!1d15857.530914116462!2d106.819091!3d-6.47311!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x0%3A0x75b84a8f7ce87bff!2sPT.%20Prolabios%20Mitra%20Analitika!5e0!3m2!1sid!2sid!4v1566724779778!5m2!1sid!2sid\" width=\"100%\" height=\"450\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\"></iframe></p>\r\n<p><strong>PT PROLABIOS MITRA ANALITIKA</strong><br />Komplek Cibinong Griya Asri Blok B2 No. 1 RT 04 RW 08 Kelurahan Tengah, <br />Cibinong &acirc;&euro;&ldquo; Bogor West Java Indonesia 16913 <br />Phone : +62 21 8792 9433, +62&Acirc;&nbsp;8128374867<br />Email : lisa.aryadi@prolabios.com / sandi@prolabios.com</p>', '', '', '', '2018-08-05 17:31:01', '2024-08-06 17:52:34', 3, '2019-09-11 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(126, 46, 0, 'Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing', '', '<p>The introduction of various antimicrobials for treating variety of infections showed the necessity of performing antimicrobial susceptibility testing as a routine procedure in all microbiology laboratories. In laboratories it can be made available by using antibiotic disk which will diffuse slowly into the medium where the suspected organism is grown. The basic principle of the antibiotic susceptibility testing has been used in microbiology laboratories over 80 years. Various chemical agents such as antiseptics, disinfectants, and antibiotics are employed to combat with the microbial growth. Among these, antibiotics are generally defined as the substances produced by the microorganism such as Penicillium, which has the ability to kill or inhibit the growth of other microorganisms, mainly bacteria. <strong>Antimicrobial susceptibility tests (ASTs)</strong> basically measures the ability of an antibiotic or other antimicrobial agent to inhibit the invitro microbial growth.</p>\r\n<p>There are many different procedures that microbiologists use to study the effects of various antimicrobial agents in treating an infection caused by different microorganisms. <strong>Mueller Hinton Agar</strong> is considered as best for the routine susceptibility testing since it is has batch-to-batch reproducibility, low concentration of inhibitors of sulphonamide, trimethoprim and tetracyclines and produce satisfactory results for most of the non-fastidious pathogens. Fastidious organisms which require specific growth supplements need different media to grow for studying the susceptibility patterns.</p>\r\n<p><strong>The Kirby Bauer test</strong> is a qualitative assay whereby disks of filter paper are impregnated with a single concentration of different antibiotics or any chemicals that will diffuse from the disk into the agar. The selected antibiotic disks are placed on the surface of an agar plate which has already been inoculated with test bacteria. During the incubation period, the antibiotics/chemicals diffuse outward from the disks into the agar. This will create a concentration gradient in the agar which depends on the solubility of the chemical and its molecular size. The absence of growth of the organism around the antibiotic disks indicates that, the respected organism is susceptible to that antibiotic and the presence of growth around the antibiotic disk indicates the organism is resistant to that particular antibiotic. This area of no growth around the disk is known as a zone of inhibition, which is uniformly circular with a confluent lawn of growth in the media.</p>\r\n<p>The diameters of the zone of inhibition are measured (including disk) using a metric scale or a sliding caliper. The measured zone diameter can be compared with a standard chart for obtaining the susceptible and resistant values. There are zone of intermediate resistance which means that the antibiotic may not be sufficient enough to eradicate the organism from the body.</p>', '', '5ee3a33cc0111005f471c1751de595aa.jpg', '', '2019-08-25 16:40:17', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 1, '2019-08-25 00:00:00', 'blog', '', '', '', 0),
(118, 61, 0, 'Endotoxin Xiamen Bioendo  - Cina', '', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Endotoxins</strong> are small bacterially-derived hydrophobic lipopolysaccharides (LPS) molecules locating in the outer cell membrane of gram-negative bacteria. Endotoxins consist of a core polysaccharide chain, O-specific polysaccharide side chains (O-antigen) and a lipid compenent, Lipid A, which is responsible for the toxic effects. Bacteria shed endotoxin in large amounts upon cell death and when they are actively growing and dividing. A single Escherichia coli contains about 2 million LPS molecules per cell.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Endotoxin can easily contaminate labwares, and its presence can significantly impart both in vitro and in vivo experiments. And for parenteral products, parenteral products contaminated with endotoxins including LPS can lead to the development of fever, induction of inflammatory response, shock, organ failure and death in human. For dialysis products, LPS can be transferred through membrane with large pore size by back-filtration from the dialysis fluid to the blood, inflammatory problems may be caused accordingly.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Endotoxin is detected by the Lyophilized Amebocyte Lysate (LAL). Bioendo has been dedicated to researching, developing and producing LAL reagent for more than four decades. Our products cover all techniques employed to detect endotoxin, which are gel-clot technique, turbidimetric technique, and chromogenic technique.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img title=\"Bioendo\" src=\"/content/photo/fb05d296cc8ab8a0e869ce18b8c7b928.jpg\" alt=\"Bioendo\" width=\"275\" height=\"64\" />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>X</strong><strong>i</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>me</strong><strong>n</strong><strong> Bi</strong><strong>o</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>nd</strong><strong>o</strong> <strong>T</strong><strong>ec</strong><strong>hn</strong><strong>o</strong><strong>l</strong><strong>ogy</strong> <strong>Co.,</strong> <strong>L</strong><strong>t</strong><strong>d</strong><strong>.</strong>, founded in 1978, is the expert in the field of endotoxins and Fungi (1,3)-&beta;-D-glucan testing. Bioendo works on promoting application and development of lyophilized amebocyte lysate, and dedicates to researching, developing, producing, and marketing amebocyte lysate for four decades. Our products are registered at CFDA (China Food and Drug Administration) since 1988. We participate in preparing national standard amebocyte lysate and Reference Standard Endotoxin and standardizing Control Standard Endotoxin for the Government of China.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Cooperating with School of Life Science, Xiamen University, Xiamen Medical College, Xiamen Ocean Vocational College, and other universities, Bioendo is excellent at R&amp;D. And supported by strong R&amp;D strength and advanced equipment, Bioendo produces high-quality Lyophilized Amebocyte Lysate and endotoxins assay kits. Bioendo&rsquo;s products mainly contain amebocyte lysate and endotoxins assay kits in gel clot technique, kinetic chromogenic, kinetic turbidimetric technique and end-point chromogenic technique, endotoxins assay kits for water and dialysate, endotoxin removal kits, clinical diagnostic assay kit for detection of fungi (1,3) &beta;-D-glucan or invasive fungal infection, and supported items for endotoxins detection like control standard endotoxin, water for bacterial endotoxins test, endotoxin-free buffers, endotoxin challenge vials.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Bioendo also provides instruments such as Kinetic Incubating Microplate Reader, dry heat incubator, laboratory water purify system, centrifuge and other accessories.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Product range from Bioendo</strong></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 92.2264%; height: 1071px;\" border=\"1\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 37px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Parameter</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 37px; text-align: center;\"><strong>Product</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 72px; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"4\"><strong>Gel Clot Endotoxin Assay</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Gel Clot Endotoxin Assay Single Test in Vials</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Gel Clot Endotoxin Assay Single Test in Ampoules</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Gel Clot Endotoxin Assay Multi-Test in Vials</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">BioendoBioendo&trade; KT Endotoxin Test Kit (Kinetic Turbidimetric Assay) GC Endotoxin Test Kit (Gel Clot Assay)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 70px; text-align: left; width: 38.5263%;\" rowspan=\"4\"><br /><strong>Endotoxin-specific Amebocyte Lysate</strong><strong><br /></strong><strong><br /></strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: left; width: 56.9237%; height: 16px;\">Gel clot technique</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Kinetic turbidimetric technique</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Kinetic chromogenic technique</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">End-point chromogenic technique</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 36px; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\"><strong>Endotoxin Test Kit for Water and Dialysate</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Rapid Gel Clot Endotoxin Assay Kit</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Endotoxin Assay Kit for Water and Dialysate (Gel Clot Assay)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><strong>End-point Chromogenic Endotoxin Assay</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Bioendo&trade; EC Endotoxin Test Kit (End-point Chromogenic Assay) 13</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 36px; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\"><strong>Kinetic Turbidimetric Endotoxin Assay</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Kinetic Turbidimetric Amebocyte Lysate Vials</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Bioendo&trade; KT Endotoxin Test Kit (Kinetic Turbidimetric Assay)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 36px; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"2\"><strong>Kinetic Chromogenic Endotoxin Assay</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Kinetic Chromogenic Amebocyte Lysate Vials</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Bioendo&trade; KC Endotoxin Test Kit (Kinetic Chromogenic Assay)</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 36px;\" rowspan=\"2\">\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Clinical Diagnostic Reagents</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Fungi (1,3)-&beta;-D-glucan Assay Kit</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;\">Endotoxin Assay Kit for Human Plasma</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.5263%; height: 136px; text-align: center;\" rowspan=\"8\"><strong>Bacterial Endotoxin Detection Accessories</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 56.9237%; height: 18px;